hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","599 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Awn and al-Fadl ibn Ghanim narrated to us, they said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from al-Ala' ibn Kathir, from Makhul, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The least of menstruation is three days and the most is ten. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except al-Ala'."
"602","600 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin and Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man will soon be concerned about who will accept his charity from him, and will not find him. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak except Sa'id."
"603","601 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, it belongs to him, and the unjust root has no right. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, except Muslim."
"604","602 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Five creatures, all of them harmful, are killed in the sacred and unsacred territory, and the pilgrim in ihram kills them: the kite, the snake, the mouse, the scorpion, and the voracious dog. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Umayyah except Ibn Abi Layla; his son is alone in transmitting it from him."
"605","603 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Qatadah was asked about a man who missed a rak'ah of the morning prayer until the sun rose, and he said: Khilas ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He prays another rak'ah in addition to it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam."
"606","604 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir, from Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself, I would bring him water, and he would clean himself with it and wipe his hand on the ground. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Zur'ah except Ibrahim ibn Jarir; Sharik is alone in transmitting it."
"607","605 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Fadl al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham Abd al-Rahman ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid al-Sadusi, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today is wagering and tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or Hell; the loser is he who enters Hell. I am first, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq is the one praying behind, Umar ibn al-Khattab is third, then people after me according to precedence, the first then the first. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Abd al-Rahman; al-Walid is alone in transmitting it."
"608","606 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Habib Abu Muhammad who said: I heard al-Farazdaq ibn Ghalib saying: I met Abu Hurayrah in Sham, and he said to me: Are you al-Farazdaq? I said: Yes. He said: Are you the poet? I said: Yes. He said: If you remain alive you will meet people who say: there is no repentance for you, so beware of cutting off your hope in Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Farazdaq except Habib; Salih al-Murri is alone in transmitting it."
"609","607 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wala' belongs to the one who emancipates; and Barirah was given meat in charity, so she gave some of it to A'ishah as a gift, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her and a gift for us. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam."
"610","608 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Ala' al-Zubaydi narrated to us, he said: Abu Awn Thuwabah ibn Awn al-Tanukhi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Sakuni, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me awake; Satan does not take my likeness. It is not known to be narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except through this channel."
"611","609 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Sa'id Abu Hafs al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Karim al-Jazari informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Jibril, from Allah the Exalted who said: Whoever humiliates a friend of Mine has openly confronted Me with war. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Sadaqah; Umar is alone in transmitting it."
"612","610 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Husayn al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my grave and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except Yahya; Abu Husayn is alone in transmitting it."
"613","611 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Hasan who said: Amr ibn al-As said: We did not think that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died on the day he died while loving a man whom Allah would then admit to Hell. It was said to him: He used to employ you? He said: Allah knows best, but he did love a man. They said: Who is he? He said: He used to love Ammar ibn Yasir. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Azhar; Abbad is alone in transmitting it."
"614","612 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Sa'id ibn Fayruz, from his father, that the delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We saw him praying in two sandals placed opposite each other. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Hammad, and it is not narrated from Fayruz al-Daylami except with this chain."
"615","613 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bahr al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Abu al-Jahm, from al-Qasim, the freed slave of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, the people fell upon garlic and began eating it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this plant should not come near our mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Abthar; Ahmad ibn Bahr is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain."
"616","614 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: al-Mut'im ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his mount on the day of sacrifice saying: Let my nation take their rites, for I do not know whether I will not perform Hajj after this year of mine."
"617","615 - And with the same chain: from Jabir who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stone the Jamrat al-Aqabah alone on the first day in the forenoon, and as for after that, at the decline of the sun."
"618","616 - And with the same chain: from Jabir who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning with pebbles like those used for khadhf. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Mut'im except al-Haytham ibn Humayd; Ali ibn Hujr is alone in transmitting them."
"619","617 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir and Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: washing on Friday is obligatory upon whoever has reached puberty among those who come to Friday prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ata', except Abd al-Rahman; Muhammad ibn Ja'far is alone in transmitting it."
"620","618 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jallalah animals: their meat, their milk, and riding them. No one narrated this hadith from Umar except Isma'il."
"621","619 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head, and a group of his Companions did, and some of them shortened. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far except Hatim ibn Isma'il; Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"622","620 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Siddiq ibn Musa, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: On the Day of Resurrection Allah Almighty will give a man from the nation of Muhammad a Jew and a Christian, and it will be said: Ransom yourself with this one from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Siddiq except Hafs."
"623","621 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Nu'man al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What an excellent condiment vinegar is. No one narrated this hadith from Muharib except Hafs."
"624","622 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn al-Hakam al-Mu'addib narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when a sturdy camel and two water-skins will be more beloved to a man than what he owns."
"625","623 - And with the same chain: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will conquer the city of Heraclius or Caesar, and divide its wealth with shields, and a cry will reach them that the Dajjal has come upon their families behind them, so they will throw down what is with them and go out and fight. No one narrated these two hadiths from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Isma'il ibn Ayyash; Nasr is alone in transmitting them."
"626","624 - Ahmad narrated to us: Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, he said: Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abi Umar al-Mu'allim, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Masruq, that he heard a man narrating from A'ishah, that she said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him. Masruq said: I said: Did you hear it from her? He said: Yes. So I traveled to Madinah, and mentioned that to A'ishah, and said: We hate death. She said: It is not like that; that is only at death: the believer sees what is for him with Allah and loves meeting Him, while the disbeliever hates death, and Allah hates him at that time. No one narrated this hadith from Bukayr except Utbah, nor from Utbah except Abu Isma'il; Abbad is alone in transmitting it."
"627","625 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Salih al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Yazid Abu Khalid, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave the mosque until I teach you a verse from a chapter that was not revealed to anyone before me except Sulayman ibn Dawud. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until when he reached the threshold of the door he said: With what do you begin your prayer and recitation? I said: With - In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. He said: It is it. Then he put out his other foot. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Buraydah except Abd al-Karim, nor from Abd al-Karim except Yazid Abu Khalid; Salamah ibn Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"628","626 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and whatever intoxicates in large amounts, its small amount is forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except al-Ashja'i; Masruq is alone in transmitting it."
"629","627 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maymun al-Qaddah narrated to us, Ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: When did you pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: While the sun was white and clear. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Abdullah."
"630","628 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Musarrih al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Maysarah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Days and nights will not pass until the happiest of people with this world is Luka' ibn Luka'. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Hafs; Makhlad is alone in transmitting it."
"631","629 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mulayhah narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon on his she-camel, and he said: Beware of treachery, for it is an evil confidant; beware of wrongdoing, for it will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection; and beware of miserliness, for those before you were destroyed by miserliness only, until they shed their blood and severed their kinship ties. It is not narrated from al-Hirmas except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Nasr is alone in transmitting it."
"632","630 - Ahmad narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and said: To proceed. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Hammad."
"633","631 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Security and health are two blessings in which many people are cheated. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Harun."
"634","632 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Nusayr ibn Abi al-Ash'ath, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking in a funeral procession, and riding a bare horse with nothing on it except its bridle when returning. No one narrated this hadith from Nusayr except Makhlad."
"635","633 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata', from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me, for no servant asks it for me in this world except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Musa."
"636","634 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hisham ibn Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Mu'adh ibn Sahl ibn Anas, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I visited Abu al-Darda' in his illness, and said: O Abu al-Darda', do you not love to recover and not fall ill? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Headache and fever afflict a person until they leave upon him not even a mustard seed's weight of his sins."
"637","635 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hisham ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from his father, from Bilal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House and prayed two rak'ahs to the left of the second pillar. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Amr."
"638","636 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, from Anbasah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you prostrate, place your palms on the ground, for the palms prostrate as the face prostrates."
"639","637 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hisham ibn Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse time, for Allah is time. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except Ibrahim, and no one narrated it from Abu al-Zubayr except Sa'id."
"640","638 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white garments, and shroud your dead in them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Muwaqqari; Ali ibn Hujr is alone in transmitting it."
"641","639 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the Jamrat al-Aqabah on the day of sacrifice in the forenoon, and stoned the rest after the decline of the sun. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ibn Idris."
"642","640 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: al-Ala' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Khalil ibn Murrah, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of my nation will not attain my intercession: an unjust ruler, and one who goes to excess in religion. No one narrated this hadith from al-Khalil except al-Ala'."
"643","641 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: my brother Mukhtar narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i who said: I saw behind Malik ibn Dinar a dog following him, so I said: What is this, O Abu Yahya? He said: This is better than an evil companion."
"644","642 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Ishaq, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: The Children of Israel said: O Musa, does your Lord Almighty create a creation and then punish them? So Allah Almighty revealed to him: Sow. So he sowed, then He said: Reap. So he reaped. Then He said: Winnow it. So he winnowed it, and the chaff gathered. He said: What is this fit for? He said: For the fire. He said: Likewise I do not punish any of My creation except one who deserves the Fire."
"645","643 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Yunus ibn Ubayd and Habib ibn al-Shahid and Humayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Men and women boasted, and Abu Hurayrah said: Women are more in Paradise than men. Umar ibn al-Khattab looked at the people and said: Do you hear what Abu Hurayrah is saying? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The first group to enter Paradise, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon, and the second, their faces like the brightest star in the sky; for each man among them will be two wives, the marrow of their shanks visible from behind the skin, and there is no bachelor in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus and Habib and Humayd except Hammad."
"646","644 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi narrated to us, from Musawir ibn Sawwar, from his grandfather Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: I visited Abu Musa while he was eating chicken meat, and he said: Come. I said: I saw it eating something filthy and I preferred not to eat it. He said: Sit, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating it. No one narrated this hadith from Musawir except Abu Hilal; Ibn A'ishah is alone in transmitting it."
"647","645 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Nasr Abu Yasir narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ayyash, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of his wives and was too tired to get up, he would strike his hand on the wall and perform tayammum. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Isma'il."
"648","646 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me three years after Khadijah. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Isma'il."
"649","647 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would have him inherit. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Ibn Abi Hazim."
"650","648 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a land called Adharah, and named it Khadirah. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abdah."
"651","649 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaydullah al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your brother whether wrongdoer or wronged; if he is a wrongdoer restrain him, and if he is wronged take for him. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Isma'il and Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi."
"652","650 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas who said: I stayed as a guest with my aunt Maymunah, and that night she was menstruating and not praying; she spread a cloak for me, placed a pillow beside her for me, and spread bedding for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from the mosque, he cast off his garment, took a cloth and wore it, then lay down beside her. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Harith except Jabalah ibn Atiyyah; Muhammad ibn Thabit is alone in transmitting it."
"653","651 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Tujibi, from Abu Mansur, the freed slave of the Ansar, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he becomes angry for Allah and is pleased for Allah; when he does that he has deserved the reality of faith. And my beloved ones and friends are those who are remembered by my remembrance, and I am remembered by their remembrance. This hadith is not narrated from Amr ibn al-Hamiq except with this chain; Rushdayn is alone in transmitting it."
"654","652 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Khawlah bint Hakim - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had married her, then deferred her among those he deferred - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: She is like a man: if she emits, she washes, and if she does not emit, she does not wash. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah except Ali."
"655","653 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spitting into his garment during prayer, then rubbing it with his finger."
"656","654 - And from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered our house - while a water-skin was hanging - and drank from it while standing. So my mother stood up, cut off the mouth of the water-skin, and said: No one will drink from it after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated these two hadiths from Sharik except Ali ibn Hakim and Minjab."
"657","655 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Maslamah Amr ibn Sa'id ibn Arkun al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah, from one who narrated to him, from Uqbah ibn Amir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever conceals an indecency, it is as if he has given life to a buried girl. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except Amr."
"658","656 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Fath Nasr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Bishr ibn al-Harith al-Hafi, he said: Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa' narrated to me, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amirah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he mentioned Mu'awiyah - and he said: O Allah, make him a guide, rightly guided, and guide through him. No one narrated this hadith from Bishr except Nasr."
"659","657 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Nasr al-Tammar Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Razin, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa' who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine, and we kissed it, and that was not disapproved. This hadith is not narrated from Salamah except with this chain; Attaf is alone in transmitting it."
"660","658 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that a blind man from the Ansar sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): mark out for me a mosque in my house so I may pray in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, while his people had gathered to him, and one man among them stayed away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What happened to so-and-so? Some of the people mentioned him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did he not witness Badr? They said: Yes, but he is such-and-such. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"661","659 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hisham ibn Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi, from Abu al-Darda' who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no guardian over three except that he will meet Allah with his right hand chained: his justice will free him, or his injustice will chain him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda' except with this chain; Sa'id is alone in transmitting it."
"662","660 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Umamah who said: A man who had committed adultery was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he asked him, and he confessed. He ordered regarding him, and he was stripped, and he was found to be thin-bodied and crippled. He said: What would beating leave of this? So he called for a palm stalk bearing one hundred shoots, and struck him a single blow. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Ubaydullah."
"663","661 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah and Attab ibn Bashir and Khattab ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abu al-Wasil Abd al-Hamid ibn Wasil, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Guardian of Islam and its people, keep me firm upon it until I meet You. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Abu al-Wasil is alone in transmitting it."
"664","662 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Abu al-Wasil Abd al-Hamid ibn Wasil, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself, from a soul that is never satisfied, from knowledge that does not benefit, and from a supplication that is not heard. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of these four. O Allah, forgive me my sins, my mistakes and my deliberate acts. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Wasil except Attab."
"665","663 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Awf al-A'rabi, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its due right will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though the scent of Paradise is found from a distance of one hundred years. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Isa."
"666","664 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said regarding: Indeed those who divided their religion and became sects, you are not of them in anything - he said: They are the people of innovations and desires from this nation. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Musa; Mu'allal is alone in transmitting it."
"667","665 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: I used to play with dolls in the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning toys. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muhammad."
"668","666 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri who said: Yahya ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Urwah saying: A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about soothsayers. He said: They are nothing. They said: O Messenger of Allah, they tell something and it turns out true. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is a word of truth which the jinn snatches, then pours it into the ear of his ally like the clucking of a hen, and they mix into it one hundred lies."
"669","667 - And from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah will grasp the earth and fold the heaven with His right hand, then say: I am the King, so where are the kings of the earth."
"670","668 - And from al-Zuhri who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that he heard Hassan ibn Thabit al-Ansari saying: O Abu Hurayrah, I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Respond on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit? Abu Hurayrah said: Yes."
"671","669 - And from al-Zuhri who said: Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik narrated to me that Ka'b ibn Malik, when Allah revealed concerning poetry what He revealed, came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has revealed concerning poetry what You know, so what do You think? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer strives with his sword and his tongue. No one narrated these hadiths from Ishaq except Attab."
"672","670 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Yunus ibn Ubayd and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to bring out unmarried young women, those behind veils, and menstruating women, so they witness goodness and the supplication of the Muslims. A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, if one of them has no garment? He said: Let her sister clothe her with part of her garment - meaning on the day of Eid. No one narrated this hadith from Habib and Yunus except Hammad."
"673","671 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: Abu Qatadah had a large lock of hair, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. He said: Honor it and oil it. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Isma'il."
"674","672 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Growth of hair in the nose is a protection from leprosy. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abu al-Rabi'."
"675","673 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a slain woman in one of his expeditions and said: She was not one to fight. Then he forbade killing women and children. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Zayd except Sharik."
"676","674 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are its possessor of two horns; do not follow one glance with another glance, for the first is for you and the second is not for you. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Hammad is alone in transmitting it."
"677","675 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumasi narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Zad han narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a sheet dyed with wars and saffron with which he would go around to his wives; when it was the night of one of them she would sprinkle it with water, and when it was the night of another she would sprinkle it with water. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Umarah; Mu'ammal is alone in transmitting it."
"678","676 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihsan narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek cupping on the seventeenth of the month, the nineteenth, and the twenty-first. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Lahi'ah except Muhammad ibn Mihsan."
"679","677 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihsan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep a white rooster, for a house in which there is a white rooster is not approached by Satan, nor a sorcerer, nor the small houses around it."
"680","678 - And from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm al-Ash'ari, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What an excellent tooth-stick is the olive, from a blessed tree; it sweetens the mouth and removes tartar. It is my tooth-stick and the tooth-stick of the prophets before me. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibrahim except Muhammad."
"681","679 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your brother whether wrongdoer or wronged; if he is wronged help him against the one who wronged him, and if he is a wrongdoer restrain him from wrongdoing. No one narrated this hadith from Khudayj except Ja'far."
"682","680 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: I have not seen anyone more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a red garment. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ayyub."
"683","681 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. None narrated it from Sharik except Ali."
"684","682 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, he said: Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Zubayd al-Yami, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; Say, O disbelievers; and Say, He is Allah, One. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Qarran."
"685","683 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nizak narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and blessings; peace be upon us and upon Allah's righteous servants; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Muhammad."
"686","684 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Mujahid, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends forth something of his children, patiently seeking reward, they will screen him from the Fire by Allah's permission. No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Abu Yahya."
"687","685 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Musa al-Juhani narrated to me, from Zadhan, from Abis al-Ghifari who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He fears for his nation six traits: leadership of boys, abundance of policemen, bribery in judgment, severing of kinship ties, regarding blood lightly, and a generation who take the Qur'an as flutes, putting forward a man who is neither the most understanding among them, nor the most learned, nor the best of them, singing to them. No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Isa."
"688","686 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Fayyad ibn Muhammad al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn al-Khattab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing house-dwelling snakes. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far except Fayyad."
"689","687 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse my Companions, for by the One in Whose hand is my soul, if one of you spent the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of them, nor half of it. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, except Zayd. And Shu'bah and the companions of al-A'mash narrated it from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id."
"690","688 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tara'ifi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not admit his wife into the bathhouse; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not sit at a table over which wine is passed around. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Uthman."
"691","689 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Darraj Abi al-Samh, from Abi al-Haytham and Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of one who learns knowledge and then does not narrate it is like one who hoards treasure and does not spend from it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"692","690 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were eating on a shield, and he sat and ate with us, and did not touch water. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Musa."
"693","691 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people of the Ansar who were laughing, and said: Increase remembrance of the destroyer of pleasures. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Hammad; Mu'ammal is alone in transmitting it."
"694","692 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Musa Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghazziyah Muhammad ibn Musa, the judge of Madinah, narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muthanna al-Ka'bi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting facing the Ka'bah, sitting in ihtiba' with his hands. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Abu al-Muthanna al-Ka'bi Sulayman ibn Yazid; Abu Ghazziyah is alone in transmitting it."
"695","693 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity in less than five awsuq, there is no charity in less than five dhawd, and there is no charity in less than five awaq. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Abd al-Warith."
"696","694 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihsan al-Ukkashi narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man naming his servant or his child Harith, Murrah, Walid, Hakam, Aba al-Hakam, Aflah, Najih, or Yasar. And he said: The most beloved names to Allah are those expressing servitude to Him, and the truest names are Hammam. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muhammad."
"697","695 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihsan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, he faced it and said: You are sacred; how great is your sanctity and how sweet is your scent; yet greater in sanctity with Allah than you is the believer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad."
"698","696 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihsan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Abdullah ibn al-Daylami, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one who sneezes sneezes, respond to him even from behind seven seas; whoever responds to a sneezer, pleurisy, molar pain, and ear pain depart from him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except Muhammad."
"699","697 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from Makhul, from Waqqas ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats a meal through a Muslim man, Allah will feed him the like of it from Hell; whoever is clothed with a garment through a man, Allah will clothe him the like of it from Hell; and whoever stands with a Muslim man in a stand of showing off and seeking repute, Allah will make him stand in a stand of showing off and seeking repute on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Baqiyyah."
"700","698 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, that a man wanted to pledge allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a trace of yellow perfume on him, so he refused to accept his pledge and said: The perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent and whose color is hidden, and the perfume of women is that whose color is apparent and whose scent is hidden. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Ramadi."
"701","699 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and a cousin of mine, while in his hand was a tooth-stick with which he was cleaning his teeth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, employ us, for we have means. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We do not wish to employ upon our work one who is eager for it. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"702","700 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Yazid ibn Zuray', nor from Yazid except Umayyah ibn Bistam; al-Abbar is alone in transmitting it."
"703","701 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And take from the standing place of Ibrahim a place of prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh except Yazid, nor from Yazid except Umayyah; al-Abbar is alone in transmitting it."
"704","702 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Five harmful creatures are killed in the sanctuary: the kite, the crow, the scorpion, the mouse, and the voracious dog."
"705","703 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died suddenly, and I think that had she spoken she would have given charity. Is there reward for her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. No one narrated these two hadiths from Rawh except Yazid, nor from Yazid except Umayyah; al-Abbar is alone in transmitting them."
"706","704 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People are mines; the best of them in the pre-Islamic period are the best of them in Islam, when they understand."
"707","705 - And with the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not initiate them with greeting, and when you meet them on a road, force them to its narrowest part."
"708","706 - And with the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to sit upon a coal, so it burns his clothes until it reaches him, is better for him than sitting upon a grave."
"709","707 - And with the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever prays over it and follows it until it is buried has two qirats. It was said to Abu Hurayrah: What are the two qirats? He said: The smaller of them is like Uhud."
"710","708 - And with the same chain: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A servant gives a date in charity from good earnings, placing it in its right place, and Allah the Blessed and Exalted accepts it with His right hand; then He keeps raising it as the best of you raises his foal, until it becomes like a mountain or more."
"711","709 - And with the same chain: From the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"712","710 - And with the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not conceal for a servant in this world except that Allah will conceal for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"713","711 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Mansur al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened the prayer, he would raise his hands to his shoulders. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Umayyah except Muslim ibn Khalid."
"714","712 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Ali al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Na'ilah narrated to me, from Umm Asim, from al-Sawda', who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, and he said: Go and dye yourself with henna, then come so I may accept your pledge. This hadith is not narrated from al-Sawda' except with this chain; Na'ilah is alone in transmitting it."
"715","713 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man supplicating with both his fingers together, so he forbade him and said: Supplicate with one of them, the right one. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Hafs."
"716","714 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: Shall I not show you how the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was? He took water in his hand, rinsed his mouth and sniffed, then took water in his hand and joined his other hand to it, and washed his face; then he took with his hand and washed his hand and forearms, then did the same with the other; then he wiped his head; then he took water in his hand and sprinkled it upon his feet, and wiped his feet with it, while wearing sandals."
"717","715 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Mu'adh ibn Abi Hawwa', from his grandmother Hawwa', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muslim women, let none of you despise giving to her neighbor, even a burnt hoof."
"718","716 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not turn away the beggar, even with a burnt hoof."
"719","717 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata', from Iyas ibn Khalifah, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, that Ali ordered Ammar to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy. He said: He washes his private part and performs ablution."
"720","718 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, will we attain our wives in Paradise? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, a man will attain one hundred virgins in a single morning. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Za'idah."
"721","719 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It does not harm one of you whether he marries with little of his wealth or much, after he brings witnesses. No one narrated this hadith from Burd except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"722","720 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and the distance between its two ends is as that between San'a' and Aylah, and the pitchers therein are as many as the stars. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah except Shuja' ibn al-Walid."
"723","721 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Harith and Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali who said: Every supplication is veiled until one sends blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Abd al-Karim al-Khazzaz."
"724","722 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn and al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far."
"725","723 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani Abu al-Asbagh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abi al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to marry a man to a woman, and said: O so-and-so woman, do you love that I marry you to so-and-so? O so-and-so, do you love that I marry you to so-and-so woman?"
"726","724 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Asbagh al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best marriage is the easiest of it. No one narrated these two hadiths from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Salamah alone transmitted them. And it is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain."
"727","725 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abu Ubayd, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever says Allahu Akbar after every prayer thirty-three times, and Subhan Allah thirty-three times, and Alhamdulillah thirty-three times, and says: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is capable of all things - completing one hundred - his sins are forgiven even if they were more than the foam of the sea."
"728","726 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: that his father owed wasqs of dates, so we said to the man: Take the produce of our palms, but he refused. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with Umar, and supplicated for blessing in it for us. So we harvested it, gave the man all that was due to him, and the estimate of our palms remained as it was. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Inform Umar. So I informed him, and he said: I knew, O Messenger of Allah, that when you supplicated for blessing in it for them, it would be blessed."
"729","727 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir: that Umm Hani narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her on the day of the Conquest, and prayed Duha as four rakahs."
"730","728 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: Umm Hani claimed that he - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - ate a shoulder and did not perform ablution."
"731","729 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh, from Abu Rafi: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from sheep meat and did not perform ablution."
"732","730 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umayyah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, some people will come out of the Fire."
"733","731 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Ziyad al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Yazid ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not part of righteousness to fast while traveling. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Said ibn Yazid; Sufyan ibn Ziyad alone transmitted it."
"734","732 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Nafi Darakht narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a lineage, and the lineage of Allah is: Say, He is Allah, the One. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Nafi alone transmitted it."
"735","733 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Husayn al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my grave and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my Hawd. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except Yahya ibn Sulaym; Abu Husayn alone transmitted it."
"736","734 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Yahya, the companion of al-Basri, narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Salih, the maker of caps, narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Abdallah ibn Mughaffal narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief. No one narrated this hadith from Salih except Maymun; Kathir ibn Yahya alone transmitted it."
"737","735 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Isa al-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Musab ibn Mahan, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ubaydallah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the son of Adam, and he placed his hand under his chin, then stretched out his hand and said: This is his hope. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Musab ibn Mahan, nor from Musab except Amr ibn Abi Salamah; Ahmad ibn Isa alone transmitted it."
"738","736 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ziyad al-Jassas narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when they are wolves; whoever is not a wolf, the wolves will devour him. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad al-Jassas except Sahl ibn Said; Ishaq ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"739","737 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted with a calamity in his wealth or in himself, and conceals it and does not complain of it to people, it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him."
"740","738 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created the Garden of Eden, He created therein what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to a human heart. Then He said to it: Speak, so it said: The believers have succeeded. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Jurayj except Baqiyyah; Hisham ibn Khalid alone transmitted them."
"741","739 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. And he used to come to us for prayer, wiping our shoulders and chests, saying: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur, from al-Hakam, except Ibrahim ibn Tahman. And Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Mansur, from Talhah himself."
"742","740 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Musa ibn Atiyyah Abu al-Jahm al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The best of that to which mounts are ridden are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth except al-Ala ibn Musa."
"743","741 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdallah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Say, He is Allah, the One, is equal to a third of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim except Ali ibn al-Jad."
"744","742 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Numan al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Huddani narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Qusamah ibn Zuhayr, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the believer is attended at death, the angels come to him with silk containing musk and bundles of sweet basil, and his soul is drawn out as a hair is drawn from dough, and it is said: O tranquil soul, come out pleased and pleasing, pleased with, and folded upon it is the silk, then it is sent up with it to Illiyyin. And when the disbeliever is attended at death, the angels come with sackcloth containing an ember, and his soul is wrenched out with severe wrenching, and it is said: O wicked soul, come out displeased, with displeasure upon you, to disgrace and punishment; and when his soul comes out and is placed upon that ember, it sizzles, then the sackcloth is folded upon it and it is taken to Sijjin. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl except Sulayman ibn al-Numan."
"745","743 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Said ibn al-Arkun Abu Salamah al-Jumahi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Khulayd ibn Dalaj Abu Amr al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The security of the people of the earth from disagreement is allegiance to Quraysh; Quraysh are the people of Allah - three times - so when a tribe of the Arabs opposes them, they become the party of Iblis. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Khulayd ibn Dalaj."
"746","744 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Ghudaydi narrated to us, he said: Rushdyn ibn Sad ibn Musbih ibn Hilal al-Mahri Abu al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Nothing renders water impure except what changes its smell or its taste. No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Salih except Rushdyn; Muhammad ibn Yusuf alone transmitted it."
"747","745 - Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Milhan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Jarir ibn Abdallah, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched an expedition, he would say: In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah; do not misappropriate spoils, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill children. This hadith is not narrated from Jarir except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone transmitted it."
"748","746 - Ahmad ibn Bashir Abu Ayyub al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdallah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. Thus Jarir ibn Hazim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah. And Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talhah. And Ibn Jurayj narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik. And Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated it from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah. And Ubaydallah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Rusafi narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Thalabah ibn Abi Malik al-Qurazi, from Abdallah ibn Amr. And Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Harrani narrated it from Salim, from his father. And the correct version, and Allah knows best, is what Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated."
"749","747 - Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Habib al-Sarraj narrated to us, he said: Hayyan ibn Abdallah Abu Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) craved dates, so a sa of ajwah was brought to him; when they brought it he disapproved of it and said: Where did you get this from? They said: We sent two sas and were given one sa. He said: Return it, return it; we have no need of it. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain, and none narrated it except Yahya ibn Main."
"750","748 - Abu Ayyub Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Muhammad ibn al-Harith informed me, he said: A man called Abu Alqamah, an ally among Banu Hashim, came, and among what he narrated to us he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Among the signs of the Hour are that miserliness and obscenity appear, the treacherous is trusted and the trustworthy is accused of treachery, garments appear which women wear, clothed yet naked, and the tuhut rise above the wuul. Is it so, O Abdallah ibn Masud, that you heard it from your beloved? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah. We said: What are the tuhut? He said: The lowliest of men and people of obscure houses, raised above their righteous ones. And the wuul are the people of righteous houses. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Hajjaj."
"751","749 - Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdallah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner before you; if you do not find me, then I am at the Hawd, and the Hawd is between Aylah and Makkah, and men and women will come with vessels and waterskins. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Hajjaj."
"752","750 - Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you intends to marry a woman, there is no harm in looking at her. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Mamar; Abd al-Razzaq alone transmitted it."
"753","751 - Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, he said: Abu Hariz narrated to me that he heard Said ibn Jubayr saying: A man asked Abdallah ibn Umar about fasting the day of Arafah, and he said: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to equate it with fasting two years. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Jubayr except Abu Hariz."
"754","752 - Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard Yunus ibn Yazid narrating from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydallah ibn Abdallah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafah to Muzdalifah, then al-Fadl rode with him from Muzdalifah to Mina; both of them narrated, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept reciting the talbiyah until he stoned the jamrah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus ibn Yazid; Jarir ibn Hazim alone transmitted it, and none narrated it from Jarir except his son Wahb."
"755","753 - Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to separate between the even and the odd prayer with a salutation, and he would let us hear it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim al-Saigh except Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari."
"756","754 - Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing has been placed for my ummah in its early morning. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except Abdallah ibn Jafar."
"757","755 - Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Basri, and Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, both saying: Harun ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), called Maymun ibn Sinbadh, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The support of my ummah is through its wicked ones. This hadith is not narrated from Maymun ibn Sinbadh except with this chain; Harun ibn Dinar alone transmitted it."
"758","756 - Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning this verse: For those who do good is the best reward and increase. He said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call: O people of Paradise, indeed you have with Allah an appointment which He wishes to fulfill for you. So they will say: What is it? Has He not whitened our faces? Has He not made our scales heavy, moved us away from the Fire and admitted us into Paradise? Then the veil will be lifted for them, and they will look at Allah, mighty and majestic; nothing will be more beloved to them than looking at Him, and that is the increase. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"759","757 - Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hudhayl ibn Bilal Abu al-Buhlul narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah narrated to us, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned the adhan for us and our freedmen, the watering for Banu Hashim, and the veiling of the Kabah for Banu Abd al-Dar. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah except al-Hudhayl ibn Bilal."
"760","758 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Shuja al-Marwadhi Mahmawayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil narrated to us, from al-Muthanna al-Attar, from Salim ibn Abdallah ibn Umar, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The night prayer is two by two; when you fear that dawn will overtake you, pray one odd rakah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muthanna al-Attar except Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad."
"761","759 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman during his Hajj, and she brought out a boy in her hand and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you is reward. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf except Ubayd ibn Jannad."
"762","760 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Arqam narrated to us, from Abu al-Jarud, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, when he gave wealth as mudarabah, used to stipulate upon its holder: he should not travel with it by sea, nor descend with it into a valley, nor buy with it a moist liver; if he does so, he is liable. So he raised his stipulation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he permitted it. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Uqbah alone transmitted it."
"763","761 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Abdallah Abu Fatimah al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Atiyyah al-Bakri Bakr ibn Wail saying: My family took me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was a young boy, and he wiped his hand over my head. He said: So I saw Abu Atiyyah black-haired in head and beard, though a hundred years had passed over him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Atiyyah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Uqbah alone transmitted it."
"764","762 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Zurah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: al-Ajlah ibn Abdallah al-Kindi narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abdallah ibn Masud, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque, with Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, Shaybah and Utbah the sons of Rabiah, Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, and Umayyah ibn Khalaf present - Abu Jahl said: Which of you will go to the slaughtered camel of Banu so-and-so and bring us its dung and throw it upon Muhammad? So the most wretched and vilest of them, Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, went and brought it and threw it upon his shoulders, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating, unmoved. Ibn Masud said: And I was standing, unable to utter a word, having no clan to protect me. When Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), heard of that, she came and removed it from her father, then faced Quraysh reviling them, and they did not return anything to her. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head as he used to raise it at the completion of his prostration; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: O Allah, upon Quraysh; O Allah, upon Quraysh; O Allah, upon Uqbah and Utbah, and Umayyah ibn Khalaf, and Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and Shaybah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the mosque, and Abu al-Bakhtari met him, with a whip at his little fingers; when he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he disapproved of his face, so he seized him and said: Come, what is wrong with you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let go of me. He said: By Allah, I will not let go of you until you inform me of your affair, for evil has befallen you. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew he would not let go of him, he informed him and said: Abu Jahl ordered, and dung was thrown upon me. Abu al-Bakhtari said: Come to the mosque; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused, so Abu al-Bakhtari took him and brought him into the mosque, then turned to Abu Jahl and said: O Abu al-Hakam, are you the one who ordered that dung be thrown upon Muhammad? He said: Yes. So he raised the whip and struck his head with it, and the men drew back from one another. Abu Jahl said: Woe to you, it is for him; Muhammad only intended to cast enmity between us and save himself and his companions. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; al-Muthanna ibn Zurah alone transmitted it."
"765","763 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Travel is a portion of torment; it deprives one of you of his sleep and his pleasure, his food and his drink. When one of you fulfills his need from his travel, let him hasten back to his family. No one narrated this hadith from Malik, from Suhayl, except Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani and Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah. And the companions of Malik narrated it from Malik, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih. And Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated it from Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salih. And Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated it from Malik, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, from Aishah."
"766","764 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi Muhammad ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Hilali narrated to me, from his father, from Kab ibn Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us in the mosque and said: Who is here? Do you hear? After me there will be rulers who act in other than obedience to Allah, mighty and majestic; whoever shares with them in their deeds and aids them in their wrongdoing is not from me and I am not from him, and he will never come to me at the Hawd; and whoever does not share with them in their deeds nor aid them in their wrongdoing is from me and I am from him, and he will come to me at the Hawd. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Musa al-Hilali except Abu Hilal al-Rasibi."
"767","765 - Ahmad ibn Bushayr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim Abu Talib narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdallah, who said: The first news that came to us in Madinah of the mission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that a woman of the people of Madinah had a follower from the jinn who came in the form of a bird until he alighted upon a trunk of theirs; she said to him: Will you not come down to us so you narrate to us and we narrate to you, and you warn us and we warn you? He said: No; a prophet has been sent in Makkah who has forbidden adultery and barred stability from us. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Aqil except Abu al-Malih al-Hasan ibn Umar."
"768","766 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Abdallah al-Bunani narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wail, from Abdallah ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The murdered one will come holding his killer, his jugular veins gushing blood, before the Possessor of Might, saying: O Lord, ask this one for what he killed me? So He will say: For what did you kill him? He will say: I killed him so that might would belong to so-and-so. It will be said: It belongs to Allah. None narrated it from Asim except Ikrimah ibn Abdallah al-Bunani of Basra; al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi alone transmitted it."
"769","767 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Habibah, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke, light was seen coming out from between his front teeth. It is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this angle with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir alone transmitted it."
"770","768 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq and Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn: that a man freed six slaves of his at death, having no wealth besides them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Atiq except Hammad ibn Zayd; al-Fayd ibn Wathiq alone transmitted it."
"771","769 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Anbasah al-Awar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn and Samurah ibn Jundub: that a man freed six slaves of his at death, having no wealth besides them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots among them, freed two and kept four in slavery. No one narrated this hadith from Anbasah ibn Abi Raitah al-Awar al-Ghanawi except Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi; al-Fayd ibn Wathiq alone transmitted it, and none of those who narrated this hadith said: from al-Hasan, from Samurah, except Anbasah."
"772","770 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and consumed their prices. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Amrah except Jarir; al-Fayd ibn Wathiq alone transmitted it."
"773","771 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of Tarwiyah at Mina the Zuhr and Asr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abthar."
"774","772 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two fierce hungry wolves spending the night in a sheepfold whose people neglected it, tearing and eating, are not quicker in corrupting it than love of wealth and honor is in corrupting the religion of a Muslim man. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari."
"775","773 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mughirah ibn Miqsam al-Dabbi, from Wasil ibn Hayyan, from Abdallah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdallah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but your companion is the close friend of Allah. And the Quran was revealed upon seven letters, for every letter thereof an outer and an inner meaning. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Jarir."
"776","774 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent after eight thousand prophets, among them four thousand from Banu Israil. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Yazid al-Raqashi, except Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir ibn Mismar; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir alone transmitted it. And Ziyad ibn Sad narrated it from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Anas."
"777","775 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Ata al-Makki, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was sleeping in the dust, and said: The truest of your names is Abu Turab; you are Abu Turab. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Tufayl except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"778","776 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Salih ibn Umar, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr Dhi Murr, from Ali, concerning His saying: Those who exchanged the favor of Allah for disbelief and settled their people in the house of ruin - the verse - he said: It was revealed concerning the two most boastful of Quraysh: Banu Makhzum and Banu Umayyah; as for Banu Makhzum, Allah cut off their root on the day of Badr, and as for Banu Umayyah, they were given enjoyment for a time. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Salih ibn Umar; Said ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"779","777 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Mina two rakahs, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman for part of his rule. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar and Abdah ibn Sulayman."
"780","778 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydallah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Qazah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, with certainty, will enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Qazah ibn Suwayd; al-Qawariri alone transmitted it."
"781","779 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a day before Tarwiyah: Our lodging tomorrow, if Allah wills, is at the right side of al-Khayf, where the polytheists swore upon disbelief. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Husayn except Abbad ibn al-Awwam."
"782","780 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: I heard Marzuq Abu Abdallah al-Shami narrating from Makhul, from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no youth who grows up in worship until death overtakes him, except that Allah gives him the reward of ninety-nine truthful ones. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Marzuq Abu Abdallah."
"783","781 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Mansur al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Hakim al-Habati al-Basri narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sulayk al-Ghatafani, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon, I entered the mosque and sat down, so he said: Have you prayed the two rakahs? I said: No. He said: Then pray them. No one narrated this hadith from Zakariyya ibn Hakim except Dawud ibn Mansur al-Qadi."
"784","782 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O Aishah, this is Jibril reciting peace upon you. So I said: And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; then she went to add, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To this the greeting ended. Then he said: The mercy of Allah and His blessings upon you, people of the house. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab except Abbad ibn al-Awwam."
"785","783 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam decays except the tailbone, and in it creation is composed on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad except Said ibn Sulayman."
"786","784 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayyah ibn Yala al-Taifi narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the pulpit with a book in his hand and said: I shall give this book to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; stand, O Uthman ibn Abi al-As. So Uthman ibn Abi al-As stood, and he handed it to him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Maqburi except Abu Umayyah ibn Yala; al-Fayd ibn Wathiq alone transmitted it."
"787","785 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayyah ibn Yala narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Amr ibn Judan: When you buy sandals, buy them new, and when you buy a garment, buy it new. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Maqburi except Abu Umayyah; al-Fayd ibn Wathiq alone transmitted it."
"788","786 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two leather socks."
"789","787 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Qadim narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Isa al-Barri narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at his face in the mirror, he would say: Praise be to Allah who fashioned my creation and proportioned it, and formed the shape of my face and beautified it, and made me among the Muslims. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Harith ibn Muslim, nor from al-Harith except Hashim ibn Isa; Sulaym ibn Qadim alone transmitted it."
"790","788 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah: that the daughter of Ghaylan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I cannot attain purity; shall I abandon prayer? He said: That is not menstruation; that is only a vein, so when the period of menstruation ends, rise from the blood, then wash and pray. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim, except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Ibn Ishaq except Amr ibn Hashim; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"791","789 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Janbi narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdallah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hajjaj; Abu Malik al-Janbi alone transmitted it."
"792","790 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between the east and the west is qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Muhammad except Abdallah ibn Jafar."
"793","791 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurz Abdallah ibn Kurz al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money of a dhimmi is the blood-money of a Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abu Kurz; Ali ibn al-Jad alone transmitted it."
"794","792 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Amr al-Anqazi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Malik, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: And among those around you of the bedouins are hypocrites, and from the people of Madinah,persisted in hypocrisy; you do not know them, We know them; We shall punish them twice, then they will be returned to a great punishment - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on a Friday as a preacher and said: Stand, O so-and-so, and go out, for you are a hypocrite; go out, O so-and-so, for you are a hypocrite; so he expelled them by their names and exposed them. And Umar ibn al-Khattab had not attended that Friday due to a need of his; Umar met them as they were leaving the mosque, so he hid from them out of shyness that he had not attended Friday, thinking the people had dispersed, while they hid from Umar, thinking he had learned of their affair. So Umar entered the mosque and found the people had not dispersed. A man said to him: Rejoice, O Umar, for Allah has exposed the hypocrites today; so this is the first punishment, and the second punishment is the punishment of the grave. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Asbat ibn Nasr."
"795","793 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you swears an oath and sees better than it, let him do that which is better and expiate for his oath. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mutamir."
"796","794 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim al-Kirmani narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is ablution from a new covered jar more beloved to you or from the vessels for purification? He said: No, rather from the vessels for purification; indeed the religion of Allah is the upright, easy one. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send to the vessels for purification, and water would be brought, and he would drink it, hoping for the blessing of the hands of the Muslims. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad except Hassan ibn Ibrahim."
"797","795 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydallah, who said: Thabit al-Araj said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: This ummah will remain in good so long as when it speaks it is truthful, when it judges it is just, and when it is asked for mercy it shows mercy. Thabit al-Araj narrated no hadith from Anas other than this, nor did any narrate it from Thabit except Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal alone transmitted it."
"798","796 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus Abu Muslim al-Mustamli narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdallah al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, commanded me to judge by oath along with a witness. None of those who narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated this wording: Jibril commanded me, except Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah."
"799","797 - And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wednesday is a day of continuous ill omen. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn Muhammad except Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah."
"800","798 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in Ramadan twenty rakahs besides the witr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Abu Shaybah, nor is it narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"801","799 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Aslam al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Mansur narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Abu Talhah saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) binding his belly with a stone from hunger, so he said: O Umm Sulaym, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) binding his belly with a stone from hunger, so prepare food for him. So she prepared a disc like a qata bird, and called the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the disc, then Umm Sulaym brought a skin, squeezed it like a date-stone of ghee, seasoned the disc with it, then supplicated for blessing in it, then said: Call the people of the mosque. So he called them, and seventy men ate from that disc, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and those in the house ate, then he sent some of it to his wives, and more remained than there had been. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Mansur except Sahl ibn Aslam."
"802","800 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdallah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father and his uncle Ubaydallah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he opened the prayer, would begin with: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydallah except his nephew Abd al-Rahman; Atiq ibn Yaqub alone transmitted it."
"803","801 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman, from al-Khasib ibn Jahdar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah: that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of poor memory, so he said: Seek help with your right hand for your memory. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Salih except al-Khasib ibn Jahdar."
"804","802 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dawlabi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave two nights after it was buried. None of those who narrated it from al-Shaybani said: two nights after, except Ismail ibn Zakariyya; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah alone transmitted it."
"805","803 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wealth is green and sweet; whoever takes it rightfully, what an excellent aid it is. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Anas except Man ibn Isa."
"806","804 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that Umm Sulaym menstruated after she had performed the farewell circumambulation, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to depart. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said; Abbad ibn al-Awwam alone transmitted it."
"807","805 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Ibn Manzur narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in attending the Isha prayer on Wednesday night, they would come to it even crawling. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Zakariyya ibn Manzur; Atiq ibn Yaqub alone transmitted it."
"808","806 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad al-Tai narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I attended Abu Bakr al-Siddiq when a man came to him and said: O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, this one wants to take all my wealth and seize it. He said to him: What do you say? He said: Yes. So Abu Bakr said: You have from his wealth only what suffices you. He said: O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You and your wealth belong to your father? Abu Bakr said: Be content with what Allah, mighty and majestic, was content with. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad."
"809","807 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, from Shubah, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he traveled, would pray two rakahs until he returned. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abu Said; Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl alone transmitted it."
"810","808 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, all of you will enter Paradise except whoever refuses and strays from Allah as a camel strays. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who refuses to enter Paradise? He said: Whoever obeys me enters Paradise, and whoever disobeys me enters the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"811","809 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dawlabi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the right upon Muslims is washing on Friday, and that a man perfume himself from his family's perfume. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if one finds no perfume? He said: Then water is perfume. No one narrated this hadith from al-Bara except with this chain; Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad alone transmitted it."
"812","810 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Dinar, from al-Amash, al-Hasan ibn Amr, Jami ibn Abi Rashid, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi and Abu Husayn, from al-Mundhir al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: I said to my father: Which people are best after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Abu Bakr. I said: Then who? He said: Then Umar. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, al-Hasan ibn Amr, Muhammad ibn Qays and Abu Husayn except Mansur ibn Dinar, nor from Mansur except Said ibn Salim; Ahmad ibn Yunus alone transmitted it."
"813","811 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Laythi, from Amr ibn Abdallah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jundai, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spread out your garment, so I spread it out; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me most of the day, then spat into my garment, then I clasped my garment to my belly, and I never forgot anything thereafter. Amr ibn Abdallah al-Jundai narrated no hadith from Abu Hurayrah other than this, and Abdallah ibn Abd al-Aziz alone transmitted it."
"814","812 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd al-Jabbar, that he heard Ibrahim ibn Jarir narrating from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it out of fear of it is not from me. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Jarir except Dawud ibn Abd al-Jabbar."
"815","813 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Qutbah ibn Malik, from Arfajah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr prayer, then said: My companions were weighed tonight; Abu Bakr was weighed and outweighed, then Umar was weighed and outweighed, then Uthman was weighed and outweighed. This hadith is not narrated from Arfajah except with this chain; Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir alone transmitted it."
"816","814 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydallah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah and Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas, who said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah, and his knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they would both cry out with both, for Hajj and Umrah together. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, except Ubaydallah ibn Amr."
"817","815 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Qays narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Hubab Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a sound that alarmed him, so Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this sound, O Jibril? He said: This is a rock that fell from the edge of Hell seventy years ago; this is when it reached its bottom, and Allah loved to let you hear its sound. After that day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen laughing heartily until Allah took him."
"818","816 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Qays narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dawn rises, there is no prayer except the two rakahs of Fajr. No one narrated these two hadiths from Yahya ibn Said except Ismail ibn Qays; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad alone transmitted them."
"819","817 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydallah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Muhammad mentioning from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the expulsion of Banu al-Nadir from Madinah, some people of them came to him and said: We have debts not yet due. He said: Reduce and hasten payment. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah; Muslim ibn Khalid alone transmitted it."
"820","818 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydallah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Friday prayer upon a traveler. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except his son Abdallah; Abu Bakr al-Hanafi alone transmitted it."
"821","819 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abdallah ibn Abi Khatham narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays six rakahs after Maghrib, speaking nothing between them, they equal for him worship of twelve years. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Umar ibn Abdallah; Zayd ibn al-Hubab alone transmitted it."
"822","820 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: And the righteous of the believers - he said: It was revealed concerning Abu Bakr and Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun ibn Mihran except Furat ibn al-Saib."
"823","821 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Idris al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Abi Hawdhah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Qartha al-Dabbi, from Salman al-Farisi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Salman, do you know what Friday is? - three times - I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Your father Adam was gathered. Then he said: But I shall inform you about Friday: whoever comes to Friday, purifies himself as commanded, then walks to the mosque, and listens attentively until he finishes his prayer, it is expiation for what came before it of Fridays. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Amr ibn Abi Qays and Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid."
"824","822 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Idris al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Sawwar and al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdallah ibn Ukaym, who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us a month before his death: Do not benefit from carrion by skin or sinew. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Abdallah ibn Idris; Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid alone transmitted it."
"825","823 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Rushdyn ibn Sad narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has refuse, and the refuse of the mosque is: No, by Allah, and Yes, by Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uqayl, nor from Uqayl except Rushdyn."
"826","824 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a boy who urinated upon him, so he sprinkled water over it; and a girl was brought who urinated upon him, so he washed it. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, except Usamah ibn Zayd; Abdallah ibn Musa alone transmitted it."
"827","825 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Hawdhah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdallah ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will soon be a people who recite the Quran, drinking it as they drink water; it will not pass beyond their throats. Then he placed his hand upon his throat and said: It will not pass beyond here. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"828","826 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Idris al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her during her Hajj: Your reward is according to your expenditure. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Mihran."
"829","827 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifah narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Abi Hind al-Ashjai narrated to me, he said: al-Harith al-Awar al-Hamdani narrated to me, he said: I was with Ali ibn Abi Talib when the son of Talhah ibn Ubaydallah came to him; Ali said to him: Welcome to you, O son of my brother, to me, here; so he seated him with him, then said: By Allah, I hope that I and your father are among those of whom Allah said: And We removed whatever rancor was in their breasts - the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind except Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifah."
"830","828 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: al-Harish ibn al-Khirrit, brother of al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from Aishah, who said: We used to place for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three covered vessels: one for his ablution, one for his tooth-stick, and one for his drink. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except al-Harish; Harami alone transmitted it."
"831","829 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Man narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubaydallah ibn Abdallah ibn Utbah, who said: Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), borrowed three hundred dirhams; her family said to her: Do you borrow while you have nothing to repay? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever contracts a debt intending in himself to repay it, Allah will aid him in it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah and Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid."
"832","830 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Raja ibn Abi Salamah Abu al-Miqdam informed me, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ishaq ibn Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Kab al-Ahbar, who said: I said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: I know a people upon whom, had this verse been revealed, would have looked to the day in which it was revealed and taken it as a festival. Umar said: Which verse? He said: Today I have perfected for you your religion - to the end of the verse. Umar said: I know on which day it was revealed: Today I have perfected for you your religion - on a Friday, the day of Arafah, and both are festivals for us. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Qabisah except Ubadah ibn Nusayy, nor from Ubadah except Raja; Zayd ibn al-Hubab alone transmitted it."
"833","831 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Buzraj, who said: Ibn Rummanah narrated to me, who said: Wabar ibn Isa al-Khuzai said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you build the mosque of Sana, place it to the right of a mountain called Din. This hadith is not narrated from Wabar ibn Isa except with this chain; Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari alone transmitted it."
"834","832 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, he said: Hazim ibn Jabalah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan al-Shaybani, from Abdallah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: Whoever prefers anyone of the Companions of the Messenger over Abu Bakr and Umar has belittled the Emigrants and the Helpers, and twelve thousand of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). None narrates this hadith from Abu Sinan except Hazim ibn Jabalah, nor is it narrated from Ammar except with this chain."
"835","833 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman, from Muhammad ibn Abi Musa, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection naked, barefoot. Umm Salamah said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, how shameful, will some of us look at others? He said: People will be preoccupied. I said: What preoccupies them? He said: The spreading of the scrolls, wherein are atoms weights and mustard-seed weights. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Said ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"836","834 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, who said: Abd al-Karim al-Basri narrated to me, who said: Alqamah ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi narrated to me, who said: I was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Bilal would bring us our breakfast in Ramadan while we were traveling at dawn, and we would say: O Bilal, has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broken his fast? He would say: Yes, by Him in whose hand is my soul; I did not come from him until he broke his fast. So he would put his hand down, eat, and we would eat; and he would bring us our suhur, uncovering the tent flap so we could see our food. This hadith is not narrated from Alqamah al-Thaqafi except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Ismail alone transmitted it."
"837","835 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Abdallah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qudamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib al-Jumahi, who said: I attended al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf beating al-Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi concerning the affair of Ibn al-Zubayr; his father Sahl came in a waist-wrapper and cloak and shouted at al-Hajjaj: Will you not observe the bequest of the Messenger of Allah concerning us? He said: What did the Messenger of Allah bequeath concerning you? He said: He bequeathed that good be done to the doers of good among the Ansar, and their evildoers be pardoned. So he released him. No one narrated this hadith from Qudamah ibn Ibrahim except Abdallah ibn Musab; his son Musab alone transmitted it."
"838","836 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Abdallah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Musab ibn Thabit, from Abdallah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of gatherings are the most spacious. No one narrated this hadith from Abdallah ibn Abi Talhah except Musab ibn Thabit."
"839","837 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Abdallah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father - Abdallah ibn Musab - narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you for whom the Fire will be forbidden tomorrow? For every gentle, soft, easy, approachable one. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abdallah ibn Musab; his son alone transmitted it."
"840","838 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution for prayer, let him not interlace his fingers. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Darawardi. And people narrated it from Ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"841","839 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: A son of al-Mundhir - Ubaydallah and Muhammad - narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves that his scroll please him, let him increase therein seeking forgiveness. This hadith is not narrated from al-Zubayr except with this chain; Atiq ibn Yaqub alone transmitted it."
"842","840 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink in three breaths; when he brought the vessel near his mouth he mentioned Allah, and when he moved it away he praised Allah, doing that three times. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except al-Darawardi; Atiq ibn Yaqub alone transmitted it."
"843","841 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdallah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father and his uncle Ubaydallah ibn Umar, from Nafi: that Ibn Umar, when he opened the prayer, would begin with: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, in the Mother of the Quran and in the surah following it, and he would mention that he heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"844","842 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Abu Abdallah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to clip his nails and trim his mustache on Friday before going to the prayer."
"845","843 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Abu Abdallah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will illuminate with radiant light on the Day of Resurrection for those who walk to the mosques in darkness."
"846","844 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Abu Abdallah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah: that when rain came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the spouts flowed, he said: No drought upon you this year, meaning famine. None narrated these hadiths from al-Agharr except Ibrahim ibn Qudamah; Atiq alone transmitted them."
"847","845 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Muammal al-Makhzumi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. We said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said - on the third or fourth time: And those who shorten. No one narrated this hadith from Abdallah ibn al-Muammal except Said ibn Sulayman."
"848","846 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn al-Muammal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Hurayrah, hold a wedding feast even with a sheep. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab except Abdallah ibn al-Muammal."
"849","847 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn al-Muammal, who said: Humayd, freedman of Afra, narrated to us, from Qays ibn Said, from Mujahid, who said: Abu Dharr came to us, seized the ring of the door of the Kabah, and called out in his loudest voice, saying: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, nor prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, except in Makkah, except in Makkah. No one narrated this hadith from Qays ibn Said except Humayd, freedman of Afra, who is Humayd ibn Qays al-Araj; Abdallah ibn al-Muammal al-Makhzumi alone transmitted it."
"850","848 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn al-Muammal, from Ata, from Abdallah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Chain knowledge. I said: What is its chaining? He said: Writing. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Abdallah ibn al-Muammal."
"851","849 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn al-Muammal, who said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Abdallah ibn al-Muammal."
"852","850 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good character melts sins as water melts ice, and bad character corrupts deeds as vinegar corrupts honey."
"853","851 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Kab mentioning from Ibn Abbas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two fierce wolves spending the night among sheep are not more corrupting to them than the love of the son of Adam for honor and wealth. These two hadiths are not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Isa ibn Maymun alone transmitted them."
"854","852 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before you is a Hawd as between Jarba and Adhruh. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Mujabbar except Said."
"855","853 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbar, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from Humayl al-Ghifari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ibn Mujabbar. And Rawh ibn al-Qasim and others narrated it from Zayd, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Basrah Humayl ibn Basrah."
"856","854 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man gives his wife water to drink, he is rewarded. He said: So I stood to her, gave her water to drink, and informed her of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abbad."
"857","855 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Abbad, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, from Asim ibn Adi: that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when this verse was revealed: Then they do not bring four witnesses. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, until they bring four witnesses? The loser has already fulfilled his need. He said: He had not stood up before his cousin, his paternal uncle's son, came with his wife carrying a boy, she saying: He is from you, while he was saying: He is not from me; then the verse of lian was revealed. He said: So I am the first who spoke of it, and the first tested with it. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Adi except al-Shabi; Husayn alone transmitted it."
"858","856 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hushaym, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, who said: Abu Jafar al-Ashjai informed me, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and loneliness of the night seized me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with you? I said: I am in this place on a dark night, and I fear for you. He said: No indeed; Allah, mighty and majestic, will send us a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love, to guard us the rest of our night. She said: While I was thus, I saw a dark figure approaching us; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this? He said: I am Sad ibn Malik; I came to guard you the rest of this night of yours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laid his head down and slept. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Jafar except al-Awwam."
"859","857 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Sufyan."
"860","858 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Idris al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Hawdhah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child of adultery will not enter Paradise, nor anything of his offspring to seven forefathers. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Amr."
"861","859 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Amr, from Furat al-Qazzaz, from Ubaydallah ibn Abbad, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed with us; when he gave salam, the people gestured with their hands right and left. He saw them and said: What is wrong with you, turning your hands right and left as if they were the tails of unruly horses? When one of you gives salam, let him greet whoever is on his right and whoever is on his left. When they prayed with him again, they did not do that. He said: And we sat with him, and he said: Islam will remain manifest until there are twelve amirs or caliphs, all of them from Quraysh. No one narrated this hadith from Furat except Amr."
"862","860 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, he said: Qazah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydallah ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Ghannam, from some of his mothers, from Umm Farwah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The most beloved deeds to Allah, mighty and majestic, are prayer at its time - or he said: at the beginning of its time. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydallah except Qazah."
"863","861 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdallah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Hafs ibn Ubaydallah ibn Anas, from his grandfather Anas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Many a disheveled, dusty one with two worn garments, turned away from people's doors, who, if he swore by Allah, Allah would fulfill it. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs except Usamah."
"864","862 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: The two sons of al-Mundhir - Abdallah and Muhammad - narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the mosque there is a spot before this pillar; if people knew, they would not pray in it except by casting lots for it - and with her was a group of his Companions and sons of the Emigrants - so they said: O Mother of the Believers, where is it? She was obscure to them; they stayed with her a while, then left, while Abdallah ibn al-Zubayr remained. They said: She will inform him of that place, so they watched him in the mosque to see where he prayed. He came out after a while and prayed at the pillar at which his son Amir ibn Abdallah ibn al-Zubayr prayed, and it was said to it: the pillar of lots. Atiq said: It is the pillar in the middle between the grave and the pulpit; to its right toward the pulpit are two pillars, between it and the pulpit are two pillars, between it and the courtyard are two pillars; it is in the middle of that, and it is called the pillar of lots. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except the two sons of al-Mundhir; Atiq ibn Yaqub alone transmitted it."
"865","863 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is among the people of Hijaz, and harshness and coarseness are in Rabiah and Mudar. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr except Ahmad."
"866","864 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When prayer and supper are present, begin with supper. This hadith is not narrated from Salamah except with this chain; Ayyub alone transmitted it."
"867","865 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu Aqil informed us, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad informed us, from Abdallah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are seven: two saving, two with their likes, a deed with ten likes, a deed with seven hundred multiples, and a deed whose reward its doer knows not except Allah. As for the two saving: whoever meets Allah, mighty and majestic, worshipping Him sincerely, associating nothing with Him, Paradise becomes due for him; and whoever meets Allah associating something with Him, the Fire becomes due for him. Whoever does an evil deed is recompensed with it; whoever intends to do a good deed but does not do it is recompensed with its like; whoever does a good deed is recompensed tenfold; whoever spends his wealth in the path of Allah, his spending is multiplied, the dirham by seven hundred and the dinar by seven hundred; and fasting - none knows the reward of its doer except Allah, mighty and majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Abdallah ibn Dinar except Umar ibn Muhammad; Abu Aqil alone transmitted it."
"868","866 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: al-Jarrah ibn Minhal informed me, from Habib ibn Nujayh, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Abdallah ibn Arqam al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every nation has a trustee, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. This hadith is not narrated from Abdallah, from Umar, except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ishaq alone transmitted it."
"869","867 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from al-Sunabihi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no servant who prostrates to Allah, mighty and majestic, a prostration, except that Allah raises him a degree thereby and removes a sin from him thereby. This hadith is not narrated from Ubadah except with this chain; Khalid alone transmitted it."
"870","868 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir, who said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhayriz, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, saying: Go until you come to Abu Bakr, finding him in his house sitting with his knees drawn up; say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites peace upon you and says: Rejoice in Paradise. Then go until you come to the pass, meeting Umar therein upon a donkey, his baldness gleaming; say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites peace upon you and says: Rejoice in Paradise. Then go until you come to the market, meeting Uthman therein selling and buying; say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites peace upon you and says: Rejoice in Paradise after severe trial. So I went and came to Abu Bakr, finding him in his house sitting with his knees drawn up as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites peace upon you and says: Rejoice in Paradise. He said: Where is the Messenger of Allah? I said: In such-and-such place. So he rose to him. Then I came to the pass, and there was Umar upon a donkey, his baldness gleaming, as the Messenger of Allah had said. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites peace upon you and says: Rejoice in Paradise. He said: Where is the Messenger of Allah? I said: In such-and-such place. So he went to him. Then I went until I came to the market, and met Uthman therein selling and buying as the Messenger of Allah had said. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites peace upon you and says: Rejoice in Paradise after severe trial. He said: Where is the Messenger of Allah? I said: In such-and-such place. So he took my hand, and we came together until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Uthman said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Zayd came to me and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites peace upon you and says: Rejoice in Paradise after severe trial. So what trial will befall me, O Messenger of Allah? By Him who sent you with the truth, I have neither sung love poetry nor wished, nor touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged to you. He said: That is it. This hadith is not narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam except with this chain; Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir alone transmitted it."
"871","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from al-Walid ibn Qays, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sabbah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, that he heard Sa'id ibn Zayd, while he was testifying concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was with him as the tenth of ten, and he said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas is in Paradise, and if I wish I will inform you of the ninth. The people said: Who is he, O Sa'id? He said: He is me, then he wept. No one narrated this hadith from al-Walid ibn Qays al-Sakuni, and he is Abu Shuja ibn al-Walid, except Muhammad ibn Talhah. And Shu'bah, al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah al-Nakha'i, Muhammad ibn Juhadah, and Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i narrated it from al-Hurr ibn al-Sabbah."
"872","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."
"873","And from Mujahid, from his freedman Abd Allah ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: I was a business partner of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the pre-Islamic era, and when I came to Madinah he said: Do you know me? I said: Yes, you were my partner; you neither disputed nor deceived. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad except Sa'id."
"874","And from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep in his prostration, and his sleep was not known except by his breathing, then he would stand up in his prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Mansur."
"875","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abu Ya'qub, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without a guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void; if he consummates with her, she gets the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part. And the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Sa'id is alone in it."
"876","Ahmad informed us, he said: Atiq ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn al-Qasim ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who said: When death approached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: O Messenger of Allah, enjoin us. He said: I enjoin upon you the first forerunners among the Emigrants, and their children after them; if you do not do so, neither an obligatory nor a voluntary deed will be accepted from you. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman except with this chain."
"877","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Atiq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty said: When My servant complains, displaying sickness before three days, he has complained of Me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Maqburi except Abd al-Rahman; Atiq is alone in it."
"878","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Atiq al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Alqamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is absent from Madinah for three days comes to it with his heart filled with aversion."
"879","And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he applied kohl, would put three sticks in the right eye and two sticks in the other, making that odd-numbered."
"880","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am a guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise for whoever abandons arguing though he is right, and a house in the middle of Paradise for whoever abandons lying though joking, and a house in the highest part of Paradise for whoever has a good inward character. No one narrated these hadiths from Abd Allah ibn Umar except Uqbah; Atiq is alone in them."
"881","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Sulayman, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits his debt, Allah will shade him in the shade of His Throne on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith except Dawud; Ishaq ibn Sulayman is alone in it."
"882","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he forbade nabidh of earthen jars, and I witnessed him when he permitted drinking it, and he said: Avoid every intoxicant. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal except with this chain; Abu Ja'far is alone in it."
"883","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Sulayman, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrating from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, that he ransomed his oath with ten thousand dirhams. Then he said: By the Lord of this mosque, if I swore I would swear truthfully; it is only something with which I ransomed my oath."
"884","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Hayyaj ibn Bistam, from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn al-As, from Muhammad ibn Zadham, from Umm Sa'd, the wife of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding the burial of blood when cupped. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Sa'd except with this chain; Anbasah is alone in it."
"885","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When (When the help of Allah comes, and the victory) was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Fatimah and said: My death has been announced to me, so she wept. Then he said: Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me, so she laughed. One of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw her and said to her: We saw you weeping, then laughing. She said: He told me: My death has been announced to me, so I wept; then he said: Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me, so I laughed. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Hilal."
"886","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The killer has no share of inheritance. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Isma'il."
"887","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Junadah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man milking a sheep and said: O so-and-so, when you milk, leave some for its young, for it is among the most dutiful of animals. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except with this chain."
"888","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Ma'mar, from Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Yusuf, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, who said: When hardship befell his family, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command them to pray, then he would recite: (And enjoin prayer upon your family and be steadfast therein). This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Salam except with this chain; Ma'mar is alone in it."
"889","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi, from Abu Sinan, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ibn Umm Maktum, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one morning and said: The Fire has been stoked, and trials have come like pieces of the dark night; if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umm Maktum except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Sulayman is alone in it."
"890","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, from Jabalah ibn Harithah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Teach me something that will benefit me. He said: When you take your bed, recite: (Say, O disbelievers), for it is a disavowal of polytheism. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah, from Jabalah, except Sharik."
"891","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Abu Shurayh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cancels a sale for his brother, Allah will cancel his slip on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Sharik."
"892","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, who said: They command me to revile my companions; rather, may Allah bless them and forgive them. And he mentioned that he was on Hira and it shook, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be still, O Hira, for there is upon you none but a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. Then he counted Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman, Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, and Sa'id ibn Zayd. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah except his son Muhammad, and Talhah did not mention in the chain between Hilal ibn Yasaf and Sa'id ibn Zayd: Abd Allah ibn Zalim."
"893","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, who said: The table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never lifted from before him with any leftover food upon it at all. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except Muhammad."
"894","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would say the talbiyah on behalf of the children and throw on their behalf. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Sa'id."
"895","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Kathir Abu Muhammad, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The debtor is imprisoned by his debt, complaining to Allah of loneliness. This hadith is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain; Mubarak is alone in it."
"896","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that an army took spoils in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consisting of food and honey, and no fifth was taken from them. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except Anas."
"897","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd Allah ibn Ikrimah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek provision in the hidden treasures of the earth. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Hisham ibn Abd Allah."
"898","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: Three men of the Ansar, none among the people was deemed to have merit over them after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, Usayd ibn Hudayr, and Abbad ibn Bishr. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Muhammad."
"899","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty loves that when one of you does a deed, he perfects it. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Mus'ab; Bishr is alone in it."
"900","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man used to lead a people in prayer, and he would recite (Say, He is Allah, the One) along with another surah in every rak'ah. His companions said to him: You recite this surah - meaning (Say, He is Allah, the One) - then you do not consider it sufficient for you, and you recite another surah with it? Either confine yourself to it, or recite the other surah and leave it. He said: I will not do so; if you are pleased, so be it, otherwise manage your affair yourselves. And he was among the best of them, and they disliked that anyone else lead them. So they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What prevents you from what your people command you, and what obliges you to this surah? He said: I love it. He said: Your love for it has admitted you to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except Abd al-Aziz."
"901","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Khalifah, from Hafs the nephew of Anas, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs except Khalaf."
"902","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Khalifah, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i narrated to me. He said: I was with al-Farazdaq in prison, and al-Farazdaq said: May Allah not save him from the hands of Malik ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Jarud if I did not go walking in Makkah, where I met Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and I asked them, saying: I am from the people of the east, and a people come out against us killing whoever says: There is no god but Allah, while sparing others. They both said to me - and if not, may Allah not save me from Malik ibn al-Mundhir - We heard our close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever kills them, for him is the reward of one or two martyrs, and whoever they kill, for him is the reward of a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Farazdaq the poet except Yahya ibn Yazid; Khalaf ibn Khalifah is alone in it."
"903","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The mightiest of your Lord's creation are ten: the mountains; iron which carves the mountains; fire which consumes iron; water which extinguishes fire; the clouds subjected between heaven and earth which carry water; wind which bears the clouds; man who shields himself from wind with his hand and goes about his need in it; intoxication which overcomes man; sleep which overcomes intoxication; and worry which prevents sleep. So the mightiest of your Lord's creation is worry."
"904","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and pressed on in travel, and he mounted before the shadow declined, he would delay the noon prayer until the first time of the afternoon prayer entered, then dismount and pray them together; then he would delay the sunset prayer until the redness of twilight began to disappear, then dismount and pray them together, the sunset and the night prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Qays except Abu Ma'shar."
"905","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Abu Hafs Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, from Ka'b ibn Malik al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and if he sits with him he immerses himself in it. This hadith is not narrated from Ka'b except with this chain."
"906","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Hafs ibn Umar, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Fresh dates were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would eat with his right hand and take the stones with his left hand, then throw them away. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah except Abu Ma'shar."
"907","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One Umrah to the next Umrah is expiation for what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz except Sa'id."
"908","Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman and Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over a funeral, while we saw the sun only on the edges of the walls. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except al-Hakam."
"909","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi, he said: Umar ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from Abu Rafi, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution, washing his face three times, washing his hands three times, wiping his head and his ears, and washing his feet three times; and I saw him another time perform ablution once once. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Rafi except with this chain; al-Darawardi is alone in it."
"910","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, he said: Abu Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two sellers have the choice as long as they have not parted. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Kathir Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman except Ayyub."
"911","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits, whoever has them, Allah will reckon him with an easy reckoning and admit him to Paradise. I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You join ties with one who cuts you, you give to one who deprives you, and you pardon one who wrongs you. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Sulayman."
"912","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Jabir, from Muslim al-A'war, from Mujahid, from Qays ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the dawn prayer when light covered the sky, the noon prayer when the sun declined, the afternoon prayer while the sun was white and clear, the sunset prayer when the fasting person breaks fast, and he would delay the night prayer. This hadith is not narrated from Qays except with this chain; Ayyub is alone in it."
"913","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Ansari, from Abu Humayd al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you proposes to a woman, there is no sin on him to look at her, if he only looks at her for the proposal, while she does not know. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Isa except Zuhayr, and it is not narrated from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi except with this chain."
"914","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah ibn Qays, who said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say concerning the saying of Allah Almighty: (It throws sparks like a palace): It is not like trees and mountains, but like cities and fortresses."
"915","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, he said: Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi and Ma'bad ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Ghasil, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has most right to the front of his mount and the front of his bed, and to lead in his own dwelling. No one narrated this hadith from al-Musayyab and Ma'bad except Ishaq, and it is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah except with this chain."
"916","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, he said: Ma'bad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: We came to Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan visiting him in illness, and he said: My sister Umm Habibah narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve voluntary rak'ahs in a day, a house will be built for him in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ma'bad except Ishaq."
"917","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Atiyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group to enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon, and those who follow them like the most beautiful brilliant star in the sky; for each man among them are two wives, upon each wife a garment through which the marrow of her leg is seen from behind the flesh, as red drink is seen in a white glass vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Fudayl."
"918","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer."
"919","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Shihab al-Hannat Abd Rabbih ibn Nafi, from Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits, whoever lacks even one of them, Allah Almighty will forgive him what is besides that: whoever dies not associating anything with Him, who was not a sorcerer nor followed sorcerers, and who bore no malice toward his brother. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Fazarah except Layth; Abu Shihab is alone in it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"920","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Sa'igh, from Ikrimah, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of martyrs with Allah is Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Hakim; Ammar is alone in it."
"921","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn al-Rabi al-Kufi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: O Messenger of Allah, do the people of Paradise sleep? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sleep is the brother of death, and the people of Paradise do not sleep."
"922","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Abd Allah al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave and said: Who is the owner of this grave? They said: So-and-so. He said: Two rak'ahs are more beloved to him than the rest of your world. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Malik except Hafs ibn Ghiyath; Hafs ibn Abd Allah is alone in it."
"923","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu al-Rabi al-Samman, he said: Asim ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat, saying: Wadinuha. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu al-Rabi."
"924","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Malik Abu Isma'il al-Qannad narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa'. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except Abu Isma'il."
"925","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: I pledge you that you associate nothing with Allah, do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, do not commit adultery, do not steal, and do not drink; whoever does any of that and its penalty is applied upon him, it is an expiation, and whoever Allah conceals, his reckoning is upon Allah Almighty, and whoever does none of that, I guarantee Paradise for him. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Tufawi; Amr is alone in it."
"926","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: Al-Mukhtar claims that revelation comes to him. He said: He spoke truly - and indeed the devils inspire their allies. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Abu Bakr."
"927","And with the same chain, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to give salam to his right and his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Abu Bakr."
"928","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn away from one another; none of you should outbid his brother, no emigrant should sell for a bedouin - leave people so Allah provides some of them from others - and no woman should stipulate the divorce of her sister. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Bakr."
"929","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Hanzalah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Hanzalah except Abbad, and it is not narrated from Maymunah except with this chain."
"930","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Bakr and commanded him to announce these words, then sent Ali after him. While Abu Bakr was on one of the roads, he heard the braying of the camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Abu Bakr came out alarmed, thinking it was the Messenger of Allah, but it was Ali. He handed him the letter of the Messenger of Allah, and made him leader of the pilgrimage season, and commanded Ali to announce these words. They went and performed Hajj, and Ali stood during the days of Tashriq and announced: The protection of Allah and His Messenger is free of every polytheist; travel in the land for four months; no polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year; no naked person shall circumambulate the House; and none shall enter Paradise except a believer. And Ali would announce them, and when his throat grew hoarse, Abu Hurayrah would stand and announce them."
"931","Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Mas'ud."
"932","And with the same chain, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Ya'la ibn Muslim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas: (And never say of anything: I will do that tomorrow, except if Allah wills; and remember your Lord when you forget) - that you say: If Allah wills."
"933","Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'ayd Hafs ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abd Allah al-Ayli, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning terrors he saw at night which came between him and the night prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Khalid ibn al-Walid, shall I not teach you words to say, which you will not say three times before Allah removes that from you? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, for I only complained of that to you hoping for this from you. He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His anger, His punishment, the evil of His servants, the whisperings of the devils, and lest they attend me. A'ishah said: Only a few nights passed before Khalid ibn al-Walid came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, by the One who sent you with the truth, I had not completed the words you taught me three times before Allah removed what I felt; I would not care if I entered upon a lion in its den at night."
"934","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'ayd narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said: O Abu Sa'id, we heard that you narrate a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning usury; clarify it for us. Abu Sa'id said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, like for like, no increase and no delay; silver for silver, like for like, no increase and no delay; and do not sell what is absent for what is present. My eyes saw and my ears heard."
"935","And with the same chain, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It is not proper for a Muslim man who has something to bequeath to let two nights pass without his will being with him. Ibn Umar said: No two nights have passed over me since I heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that my will is with me."
"936","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'ayd narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abd Allah al-Ayli, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, who said: I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when evening came upon him in my house, say: We have entered evening and the dominion belongs to Allah; praise, power, strength, ability, and authority are in the heavens and the earth, and everything belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, by You we enter morning, by You we enter evening, by You we live, by You we die, and to You is the return. And when morning came he would say: We have entered morning and the dominion belongs to Allah; praise, strength, power, ability, and authority are in the heavens and in the earth, and everything belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, by You we entered evening, by You we enter morning, by You we live, by You we die, and to You is the resurrection."
"937","And from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the istikhara, saying: One of you says: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, I seek ability from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty; for You decree and I do not decree, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If such-and-such - naming the matter by its name - is good for me in my religion and my livelihood, good for me in the outcome of my affair, and good for me in all matters, then decree it for me and bless me in it; and if other than that is better for me, then decree good for me wherever it is and make me pleased with it."
"938","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'ayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from his father, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped on his crown and between his shoulders, and would say: Whoever lets flow any of this blood, it will not harm him not to treat himself with anything for anything."
"939","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'ayd narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salamah or Hafsah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It is not lawful for a woman to mourn over anyone for more than three days, and she mourns over her husband for her waiting period until her waiting period ends. No one narrated these hadiths from Abu Mu'ayd except Amr. And none narrates the hadith of Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not proper for a Muslim man who has something to bequeath, from Sulayman, except Abu Mu'ayd."
"940","Ahmad ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, who said: We went out with the women with whom we had contracted temporary marriage, until we came to Thaniyyat al-Rikab. We said: O Messenger of Allah, these are the women with whom we contracted temporary marriage. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are forbidden until the Day of Resurrection. So they bid us farewell there, and it was therefore called Thaniyyat al-Wada; before that it was only Thaniyyat al-Rikab."
"941","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, that al-Rubayyi bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, and she brought him a cup holding about a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a quarter, for his ablution. She said: I poured upon his hands three times, then he took the vessel from me and placed it, then rinsed his mouth and nose, washed his face three times three times, washed his hands three times three times, wiped his head twice, and his ears outwardly and inwardly, then washed his feet. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except Sadaqah; Amr is alone in it."
"942","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Murrah narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, pray one odd rak'ah."
"943","And with the same chain, from Ibrahim ibn Murrah, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, Abu Bakr succeeded him, and those Arabs who disbelieved disbelieved, Umar said: O Abu Bakr, how do you fight the people, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; whoever says: There is no god but Allah, his wealth and life are protected from me except by its right, and his reckoning is upon Allah? Abu Bakr said: I will surely fight whoever separates prayer from zakat; by Allah, if they withheld from me a young goat they used to render to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would fight them over withholding it. Umar said: By Allah, it was only that I saw Allah had opened Abu Bakr's breast to fighting, so I knew it was the truth. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibrahim except Sadaqah."
"944","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Paradise was forbidden to the prophets until I enter it, and forbidden to the nations until my nation enters it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibn Aqil, nor from Ibn Aqil except Zuhayr, nor from Zuhayr except Sadaqah; Amr is alone in it."
"945","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah narrated to us, from al-Asbagh, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Secret charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord; good deeds protect from evil deaths; joining kinship increases lifespan and protects from poverty. And say often: There is no power nor strength except with Allah, for it is a treasure among the treasures of Paradise, and in it is cure for ninety-nine diseases, the least of them worry. No one narrated this hadith from Bahz except al-Asbagh, nor from al-Asbagh except Sadaqah; Amr is alone in it."
"946","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Mus'ab, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have relatives whom I join while they cut me, I do good to them while they do evil to me. He said: If it is as you say, there will remain with you a supporter from Allah Almighty against them."
"947","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Salim al-Khayyat, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin say: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into his ablution water until he pours over it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"948","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of the vessel of one of you, when a dog laps in it, is to wash it seven times, the first with earth."
"949","And I heard Abu Hurayrah say: A man called out to the Messenger of Allah, saying: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you have two garments?"
"950","And from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call for prayer is made, none of you should come to it running; let him come with calmness and dignity, pray what he catches, and make up what he misses."
"951","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever forgets and eats or drinks while fasting, let him complete his fast, for it is Allah Almighty who fed him and gave him drink."
"952","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: A good deed is ten like it; fasting is Mine and I reward for it; the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter with Allah than the scent of musk."
"953","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels curse one of you when he points at his brother with iron, even if he is his full brother."
"954","And I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin say: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two garments and two sales: that a man walk in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part, or wrap himself in a single garment then raise it upon his shoulder; and touching and casting."
"955","And from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the caravans; whoever meets them and buys anything from them, its owner has the choice when he comes to the market."
"956","And with the same chain, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me; Satan does not take my likeness."
"957","And from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When time draws near, the dream of the believer hardly lies; the truest of them in dreams are the truest in speech; the dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood; the good dream is glad tidings from Allah; the dream in which a man talks to himself; and wet dreams are from Satan. When one of you sees what he dislikes, let him not narrate it."
"958","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim told no lie except three lies: two concerning Allah - his saying: I am sick, and his saying: Rather, the biggest of them did it - and he passed through a land with a tyrant among tyrants, with Sarah with him, so he sent to him: Who is this woman to you? He said: She is my sister. So he sent to him: Send her to me."
"959","And from Salim, he said: I heard al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin say: We heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay prayer in heat, for intense heat is from the breath of Hell."
"960","And from Salim, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: There will be rulers after me who delay prayer from its time. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what should one who lives to see them do? He said: Pray the prayer at its time, and when you attend prayer with them, pray."
"961","He said: And I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin narrating from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I asked A'ishah: How did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? She said: When he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting, and when he prayed standing, he bowed standing."
"962","And I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin narrating from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I asked A'ishah about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He would fast until we said: He has fasted, and break fast until we said: He has broken fast. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fasted a complete month since he came to Madinah, except the month of Ramadan."
"963","And from Salim, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rak'ah at the end of the night."
"964","And from Salim, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Dharr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No two Muslims lose three children who have not reached puberty, except Allah admits them to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy upon them; and no Muslim spends two pairs of wealth in the path of Allah, except the gatekeepers of Paradise hasten to him."
"965","And from Salim, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin narrating from Abu Bakrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at Mina, saying in his sermon: What day is this? We fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Is this not the day of sacrifice? We said: Yes. He said: What month is this? We fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Is this not Dhu al-Hijjah? We said: Yes. He said: What land is this? We fell silent until we thought he would name it other than its name. He said: Is it not the sacred land? We said: Yes. He said: Your blood, wealth, and honor are sacred upon you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Let the present convey to the absent, for perhaps he conveys it to one more comprehending or more retentive than him. Behold, do not return after me astray, striking one another's necks."
"966","And from Salim, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Imran ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: A man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving six slaves, with no wealth besides them, and he freed them at his death. That was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who cast lots among them, freed two, kept four enslaved, freeing by lot."
"967","And from Salim, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: A'ishah was asked about what makes bathing obligatory. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man sits between the four limbs of a woman, and circumcision touches circumcision, bathing has become obligatory."
"968","He said: And I heard al-Hasan say: Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, I comb my hair, braiding my head in a tight braid; how shall I bathe from major impurity and menstruation? He said: Pour over your head three handfuls with your hands."
"969","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin narrating from Imran ibn al-Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment: they do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not take omens, and rely upon their Lord."
"970","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woman is like a rib; if you straighten her you break her, and if you leave her you enjoy her despite crookedness."
"971","And from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: Gabriel came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Allah commands you to supplicate with these words, for He will grant you one of them: O Allah, I ask You the hastening of Your well-being, patience upon Your trial, and exit from the world to Your mercy."
"972","And with the same chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give one salam to his right in prayer."
"973","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, and Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi, that Abd Allah ibn Umar divorced his wife - while menstruating - a single divorce in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take her back, then keep her until she is pure, then she menstruates another menstruation with him, then keep her until she is pure; if he wishes to divorce, let him divorce her before touching her, for that is the waiting period Allah Almighty commanded."
"974","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah provides with a righteous wife has helped him with half his religion; let him fear Allah in the second half."
"975","And with the same chain: Zuhayr said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt."
"976","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr and Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu Burdah, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: My nation is a nation shown mercy; Allah has placed its punishment in its own hands. When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will hand to every Muslim man a man of the other religions, who will be his ransom from the Fire."
"977","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Mujahid, from Juwayriyah, the wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: O Prophet of Allah, I wished to free this boy, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather give him to some of your aunts in the desert to herd for them, for it is greater for your reward."
"978","And Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None narrates to the people except a commander, or one commanded, or one showing off."
"979","And Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Husayn, from Harami ibn Abd Allah al-Waqifi, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Khatmi, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah Almighty is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"980","And with the same chain: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, that a people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and addressed. The people marveled at their speech, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Speak your speech, for some eloquence is magic, and splitting of speech is from Satan."
"981","And with the same chain, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not look at one who drags his lower garment out of pride."
"982","And Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt."
"983","And with the same chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."
"984","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt and over her maternal aunt; two garments: the samm garment, and a man sitting wrapped in a garment with nothing of it over his private part; fasting the day of sacrifice and the day of breaking fast; and prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and after the afternoon until the sun sets."
"985","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him come with calmness; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"986","And with the same chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who wears men's clothing and the man who wears women's clothing."
"987","And with the same chain, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him bathe; and whoever carries him, let him perform ablution."
"988","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the hadith. (Text abbreviated in source.)"
"989","And with the same chain: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Jabir, that he heard Ka'b al-Ahbar say: When Allah Almighty spoke to Musa in tongues before his tongue, Musa began saying: My Lord, I do not understand this, until He spoke to him in the last of the tongues before his tongue. He said: My Lord, is there any of Your creation resembling Your speech? He said: No. He said: The nearest of My creation in resemblance to My speech is the most intense sound heard from thunderbolts."
"990","And with the same chain: Zuhayr and Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not snatch knowledge from people by snatching it from them, but takes knowledge by taking scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders; they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, going astray and leading astray."
"991","And with the same chain: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Ibn Jarir, from Umayr ibn Mughallis, from Abu Najih, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is well-off enough to marry, then does not marry, is not of me."
"992","And with the same chain: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Harith ibn Mukhallad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty does not look at a man who approaches his wife in her back passage."
"993","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah Almighty made mercy one hundred parts; He kept ninety-nine parts with Him, and sent down one part to earth. From that part, creatures show mercy, so that a mare lifts her hoof from her foal fearing to strike it."
"994","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Fudayl narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Juhayfah, from Ali, who said: The best of this nation after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar."
"995","And with the same chain, from al-Haytham, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Fudayl ibn Jarir, from Muslim ibn Mikhraq, from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats us is not of us."
"996","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed an aqiqah for himself after he was sent as a prophet."
"997","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I joke, but I speak only truth. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak except al-Haytham."
"998","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings."
"999","Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us in Egypt, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Khalifah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"1000","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seek growth for orphans in their wealth, lest zakat consume it."
"1001","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Fudayl narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Safwan, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the Ansar, it is by my love that he loves them; and whoever hates the Ansar, it is by my hatred that he hates them."
"1002","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Awf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's paternal uncle is the like of his father; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened two years' charity from al-Abbas in one year."
"1003","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: Knowledge is three: a speaking Book, an established Sunnah, and I do not know."
"1004","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be dutiful to your fathers, your sons will be dutiful to you; be chaste, your women will be chaste."
"1005","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to me, he said: Uthman ibn Rabi'ah narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not meet the enemy at the start of the day, he would delay until winds blew and prayer times came. And he would say: O Allah, by You I attack, by You I move, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah."
"1006","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, I shall surely raid Quraysh, then he said: If Allah wills, then he said: By Allah, I shall surely raid Quraysh, then he said: If Allah wills, then he said: By Allah, I shall surely raid Quraysh, then he said: If Allah wills."
"1007","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Aslam ibn Abi al-Dummal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no claiming in Islam; whoever claimed in the pre-Islamic era, I have joined him to his tribe. And whoever claims a child not from his lawful union neither inherits nor is inherited from."
"1008","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Imran al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best? He said: An easy upright creed."
"1009","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Muslim, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Women have nothing in contracting marriage; Maymunah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Fadl, who entrusted it to al-Abbas, who married her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1010","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the prostration of Surah Sad: Dawud the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated it in repentance, and we prostrate it in gratitude."
"1011","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Huraym ibn Uthman Abu al-Muhallab narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Sa'dan ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Praise be to Allah before everyone, and praise be to Allah after everyone, and praise be to Allah in every state, is given reward like the worship of one who worshipped Allah Almighty."
"1012","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami of Banu Samah ibn Lu'ayy of Quraysh narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, that when a matter distressed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: There is no god but Allah, the Magnificent, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and the earth, and Lord of the Mighty Throne."
"1013","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Saffar narrated to me, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, or he was asked: Which charity is best? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which charity is best? He said: Water. I said: O Prophet of Allah, which charity is best? He said: Water. Do you not see the people of the Fire, when they seek help from the people of Paradise, saying: (Pour upon us some water or of what Allah has provided you)."
"1014","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: My father Sulayman ibn Ali narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever holds his Muslim brother's stirrup, neither hoping from him nor fearing him, Allah forgives him."
"1015","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Harb al-Shaqari narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy slaves, but beware of the Zanj, for their lives are short and their provisions scant."
"1016","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hafs narrated to us, he said: Murajja ibn Raja narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Bushayr ibn Kab al-Adawi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The master of seeking forgiveness is that you say: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You; You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can; I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done; I acknowledge Your blessing upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. Whoever says it after evening falls, then dies in that night, will enter Paradise; and if he says it after morning, after waking from sleep, will enter Paradise."
"1017","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj and Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri narrated to us, they said: Qazah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend your dying ones, close the eyes, for the sight follows the soul; and speak good, for the angels say Amen to what the people of the house say."
"1018","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Attar al-Himsi narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn Bakr, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I entered between his shirt and his skin, and I kissed from him the place of the seal, and I said: What is it that it is not lawful to withhold? He said: Salt. He said: I said: Then what? He said: Water and fire."
"1019","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deliberation, moderation, and good demeanor are one part of twenty-four parts of prophethood."
"1020","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding a door of the mosque: If only we left this door for women. Nafi said: So Ibn Umar never entered through it until he died."
"1021","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I was among those who hastened with the luggage of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of Muzdalifah."
"1022","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Kabah, in which there were six pillars, and he supplicated at each pillar, and did not pray."
"1023","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sulaym al-Sawwaf narrated to me, he said: Humayd ibn Ziyad Abu Sakhr narrated to me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us this supplication as he used to teach us a surah of the Quran: I seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death."
"1024","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Qatadah narrated to him, that Abu al-Tufayl al-Bakri narrated to him, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching any but the two Yemeni corners."
"1025","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Muhammad al-Bunani al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Malik Abu Ismail al-Qannad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cutting off is for a quarter of a dinar and above."
"1026","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Tarif ibn Zayd al-Harrani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grows a white hair in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1027","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Habib, the scribe of Malik, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah, son of the brother of al-Zuhri, narrated to us, from his uncle Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever preserves my regard with respect to my Companions will come to my Basin; and whoever does not preserve my regard with respect to my Companions will not see me on the Day of Resurrection except from afar."
"1028","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Thawban narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Urwah al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us, when we began the prayer, to say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god besides You. And Umar ibn al-Khattab used to do that; and Umar used to teach us and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say it."
"1029","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Rafi, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bid farewell to a man among his Companions, he said: May Allah provide you with piety, and forgive you your sin, and grant you good wherever you turn."
"1030","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bakr ibn al-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Abu Rawh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: Samurah ibn Jundub said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) many times, and from Abu Bakr many times, and from Umar many times? I said: Yes. He said: Whoever says in the morning and in the evening: O Allah, You created me, and You guide me, and You feed me, and You give me drink, and You cause me to die, and You give me life — he does not ask for anything but Allah gives it to him. He said: Then I met Abdullah ibn Salam, and I said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah many times, and from Abu Bakr many times, and from Umar many times? He said: Yes; so I narrated to him this hadith, and he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); these words Allah Almighty had given to Musa, peace be upon him, and he used to supplicate with them every day seven times, and he would not ask Allah Almighty for anything but He gave it to him."
"1031","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Qutaybah al-Rifai narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is offered an excuse and does not accept it will not come to my Basin."
"1032","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the people pollinating the palm trees, and said: What is wrong with the people? He said: They are pollinating, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No pollination, or: I do not see pollination as anything. He said: So they abandoned pollination, and the dates of the people came out as shis (poor, unpollinated). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am not a farmer nor the owner of palm trees; pollinate."
"1033","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed me, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dinar you spend on yourself in the path of Allah, and a dinar you spend on your horse in the path of Allah, and a dinar you spend on your family in the path of Allah; the best of them is the dinar you spend on your family."
"1034","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to me, from Abu Atiyyah, he said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith visited us, and we said: If only you would lead us in prayer. He said to us: Let your imam lead; and I shall inform you of what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you visits his brother, let him not lead him in prayer, but let one of them lead."
"1035","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabrah, from Nafi ibn Malik, he said: My father Suhayl narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm nor reciprocal harm."
"1036","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man does not give his charity until he releases himself from the jaws of seventy devils."
"1037","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sinan, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels continue to pray for one of you as long as his table remains laid out."
"1038","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Khalid Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Sayfi narrated to us — and he had reached one hundred and twelve years of age — from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqbah al-Juhani, from his father, and he had been struck by an arrow alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No Muslim who saw me will enter the Fire, nor one who saw one who saw me, nor one who saw one who saw one who saw me."
"1039","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn Awf al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came upon a pond; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted and we dismounted, and the prayer came. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bilal, stand and call the adhan. So Bilal went and poured out water, then came to the pond, and washed his face and hands, and reached toward his khuffs, and he was wearing two black khuffs, and that was before the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called to him: O Bilal, wipe over the khuffs and the head covering."
"1040","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Zamah ibn Salih, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prohibit the meat of domestic donkeys."
"1041","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was above the wafrah and below the jummah."
"1042","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drove one hundred garlanded sacrificial camels in the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"1043","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me ahead with his luggage from Muzdalifah."
"1044","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that his father was killed by the polytheists on the day of Uhud, then they mutilated him, and cut off his nose and ear. Jabir said: So I kept looking at him and at what had been done to him, and the Ansar came and covered him with a garment; then I uncovered the garment, and when I saw what had been done to him I cried out. So the Ansar came and covered him with the garment, and the Ansar went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not see what Jabir is doing? He said: Leave him, for by Allah, the angels have not ceased shading him with their wings. Then after that, I said: O Prophet of Allah, my father left a debt upon him. He said: When the dates ripen, inform me. So when the dates ripened I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he supplicated for him; and there was in his dates a surplus over his debt, and a surplus equal to what used to remain."
"1045","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night in the month of Ramadan and prayed in the mosque, and men prayed behind him following his prayer; and the people awoke in the morning and spoke of that, until when the second night came he went out and prayed in the mosque. Then when the third night came he did not go out; so the people shouted and knocked on his door, but he did not go out. Then in the morning he said: Your place was not hidden from me, but I feared it would be made obligatory upon you, and you would not uphold it."
"1046","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me a surah to recite; and while I was sitting in the mosque I heard a man reciting contrary to my recitation, and he mentioned it."
"1047","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Qazah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought some dates, and he said: This is not from our dates. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I sold two sas of our dates for one sa of these dates. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is usury; return it, then sell from our dates and buy for us from these."
"1048","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that doors be closed, saying: In the name of Allah; and if you find nothing but a stick, then lay it across it, and say: In the name of Allah; and extinguish the lamp, saying: In the name of Allah."
"1049","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"1050","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides iftar for a fasting person will have the like of his reward, without diminishing anything from his reward."
"1051","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Abd al-Karim, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah informed him, from his uncle, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you take my kunyah."
"1052","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ubaydullah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqyah for every poisonous sting."
"1053","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: I read to Maqil ibn Ubaydullah, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Magians, and said: They let their mustaches grow long and shave their beards, so oppose them."
"1054","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ufayr ibn Madan narrated to us, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on one of his campaigns, and passed by some Arab households, and sent to them: Is there any water for the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: We have no water except in a dead skin tanned with milk. So he sent to them: Its tanning is its purification. So it was brought, and he performed ablution, then prayed."
"1055","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, when a man said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the fitrah. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has come out of the Fire. So we hastened to him, and behold, he was the owner of livestock; the prayer had come, so he called it."
"1056","And with it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man being punished in his grave because of tale-bearing, and passed by a man being punished in his grave because of urine."
"1057","And with it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pawned his armor with a Jew, and took barley for his family in exchange."
"1058","And with it: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In the morning there was not in the household of Muhammad a sa of grain nor a sa of dates, though he had nine wives."
"1059","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran al-Hajabi narrated to us, from his grandmother Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, she said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A boy was born to me, so I named him Muhammad and gave him the kunyah Abu al-Qasim, and it was mentioned to me that you would dislike that. He said: What is it that made my name lawful and my kunyah unlawful, and what is it that made my kunyah unlawful and my name lawful? No one narrated this hadith from Safiyyah except Muhammad ibn Imran, and it is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain."
"1060","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I am the master of mankind on the Day of Resurrection; my Lord Almighty calls me, and I say: At Your service and blessedness, and good is in Your hands; blessed are You and exalted; at Your service, O Compassionate; and the guided is whom You guide; Your servant is before You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; blessed are You and exalted. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Musa."
"1061","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by an oath along with a witness. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shuayb except Muhammad ibn Abdullah; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1062","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, the people of Makkah said: The companions of Muhammad are hungry and emaciated. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to trot around the House, to show them that they were not so, and that they were strong and well; and they used to trot three circuits and walk four. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab ibn Bashir."
"1063","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir — a shaykh from the people of al-Raqqah — narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intend to command my youths to gather bundles of firewood... the hadith."
"1064","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Yazid al-Awar narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Qawwas narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Blessed and Exalted said: Run your fingers through your beards. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya except Said ibn Yazid; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1065","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Khattab ibn Salih, freedman of the Ansar, from his mother Sallamah bint Maqil, a woman from Qays Aylan, she said: My uncle brought me to Madinah in the pre-Islamic era, and sold me to al-Hubab ibn Amr — the brother of Abu al-Yasar ibn Amr — and I bore him Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab; then he died, and his wife said: Now, by Allah, you will be sold for his debt. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman from Qays Aylan; my uncle brought me to Madinah in the pre-Islamic era, and sold me to al-Hubab ibn Amr, and I bore him Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab, then he died, and his wife said: Now you will be sold for his debt. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the guardian of al-Hubab? It was said: His brother Abu al-Yasar. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him and said: Free her; and when you hear of captives coming to me, come to me and I shall compensate you for her. So they freed me. Then captives came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he compensated them with a boy in exchange for me. This hadith is not narrated from Sallamah bint Maqil except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1066","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is ithmid (antimony), for it grows hair, removes impurities, and clarifies vision. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1067","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zamah ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, and I was with him among a group of Muslims, Bilal called him to prayer, and he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Abdullah ibn Zamah said: So I went out, and Umar was among the people, while Abu Bakr was absent. So I said: O Umar, stand and lead the people in prayer. So he stood and said the takbir; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice, and Umar was a loud-voiced man, so he said: Where is Abu Bakr? Allah and the Muslims refuse that — twice. So he sent for Abu Bakr, and he came after Umar had prayed, and led the people in prayer. Abdullah ibn Zamah said: Then Umar said to me: Woe to you, what did you do to me, O son of Zamah? By Allah, I thought when you commanded me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had commanded you with that; had it not been for that I would not have led the people in prayer. I said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah did not command me, but when I did not see Abu Bakr I saw you as the most deserving of those present to lead the people in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad, and it is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Zamah except with this chain."
"1068","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, that Aishah narrated, she said: The last covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Two religions shall not remain in the Arabian Peninsula. No one narrated it from Salih except Muhammad."
"1069","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Majid al-Madani narrated to us, he said: I heard Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Aslami mention that his father informed him, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man of camels, tending them; I travel upon them, and this month sometimes meets me while I find strength, and I prefer to fast, O Messenger of Allah, as it is easier for me than to delay it and have it as a debt; shall I fast it, O Messenger of Allah, or break fast? He said: As you wish, O Hamzah. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah except Muhammad; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1070","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his mother, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Blessed and Exalted is jealous on behalf of the Muslim, so be jealous."
"1071","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Asma, from Anas, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crying out for Hajj; then when we arrived at Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to make it Umrah, and said: Had I foreseen what I now look back upon, I would have made it Umrah; but I drove the sacrificial animals, and joined Hajj and Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah and al-Amash; Ammar ibn Ruzayq alone narrated it from al-Amash."
"1072","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn al-Muttalib, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a striped silk garment; so I wore it, and came in the morning to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he saw it on me, he said: I did not clothe you with it to wear it; I only sent it to you to clothe women with it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Amr."
"1073","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Saib, he said: Busr ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, from al-Nawwas ibn Saman, he said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Jada, was stolen. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If Allah returns her to me, I shall thank my Lord Almighty. So she fell into a clan of Arab clans in which there was a Muslim woman; and the camels, when they grazed, grazed singly, and when the camels knelt, they knelt singly, placing their chests down. So Allah cast into her mind to flee upon her; so she saw heedlessness from the people, sat upon her, then moved her, and arrived with her at Madinah by morning. When the Muslims saw her they rejoiced with her, and walked beside her until they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw her, he said: Praise be to Allah. So the woman said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah saved me upon her, I would slaughter her and feed her meat to the poor. He said: Evil is what you rewarded her with; you have no vow except concerning what you own. So they waited, whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would introduce a fast or a prayer; and they thought he had forgotten, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, you had said: If Allah Almighty returns her to me, I shall thank my Lord Almighty. He said: Did I not say: Praise be to Allah? This hadith is not narrated from al-Nawwas except with this chain; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1074","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Qazah, from Abu Said, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the two rakahs after Asr. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Zuhayr."
"1075","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Nufay ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Umar, he said: Hudhayfah wore new clothes, and said: Praise be to Allah who covered my nakedness and beautified me among His servants. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wore new clothes, used to say the like of that. This hadith is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain; Zayd alone narrated it."
"1076","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salih ibn Ibrahim, from his father Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I arrived at Basrah, and met Abu Bakrah, and he said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every town entered by the terror of the Dajjal except Madinah; he comes to it to enter it, but finds at its gate an angel with unsheathed sword, who turns him away from it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"1077","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Wasil, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Sadi, one of Banu Bahdalah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man from my ummah will emerge who speaks by my sunnah; Allah Almighty will send down rain from the sky for him, and the earth will bring forth its blessings for him; the earth will be filled through him with equity and justice, as it was filled with tyranny and injustice; he will rule over this ummah seven years, and will descend upon Bayt al-Maqdis. A group narrated this hadith from Abu al-Siddiq, but none of those who narrated it placed anyone between him and Abu Said except Abu Wasil."
"1078","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while in Makkah, when he recited the Quran would recite aloud; so the polytheists would drive people away from him, saying: Do not listen to this Quran and make noise therein that you may overcome. And when he concealed his recitation, those who loved to hear the Quran could not hear. So Allah Almighty revealed: And neither recite aloud in your prayer nor recite it in a low tone, but seek a way between that. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Muhammad."
"1079","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Aidh, from Abu Ruwayyah, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, from Aishah, that a Jewish woman entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Aishah, and said: Death be upon you. So I said: Death and curse be upon you."
"1080","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"1081","And from Anas, that a man invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to barley bread and rancid melted fat."
"1082","And from Anas, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar, and behind Uthman; and they used to begin the recitation with: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"1083","And from Anas, he said: Seven of the companions of the Messenger of Allah would suck a single date, and they ate tree leaves until the corners of their mouths swelled."
"1084","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Khulayd narrated to us, from Maruf ibn Abi Maruf, from Abu al-Hajjaj, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alone in his house, he would be in the service of his family. No one narrated these hadiths from Khulayd except al-Nufayli."
"1085","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Urayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that this verse was revealed: Those who spend their wealth by night and day, secretly and openly — that it was revealed concerning spending on horses in the path of Allah."
"1086","And with it: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection; and their owners are aided in maintaining them; and the one who spends on them is like one stretching his hand with charity; and their urine and dung will be for their owners, with Allah on the Day of Resurrection, of the musk of Paradise. These two hadiths are not narrated except with this chain; Said ibn Sinan alone narrated them."
"1087","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid, from his father, from his grandfather — and he had companionship with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a station has been decreed for a servant from Allah Almighty which he does not reach by his deeds, Allah afflicts him in his body, or in his wealth, or in his child; then He grants him patience over that, until He brings him to the station decreed for him from Allah Almighty. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Khalid except with this chain; Abu al-Malih alone narrated it."
"1088","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn Ruwaym narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When my ummah deems six things lawful, destruction will be upon them: when cursing one another appears among them, and they drink wines, and wear silk, and take singing girls, and men suffice themselves with men, and women with women. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah except Abbad; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1089","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Safwan al-Ansari informed me, from Abdullah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The promised day is the Day of Resurrection, and the witnessed day is the day of Arafah, and the witnessing day is Friday; the sun has neither risen nor set upon a day better than Friday; and in it there is an hour in which no Muslim asks Allah for good but He answers him, nor seeks His refuge from anything but Allah grants him refuge. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Rafi except Ayyub; Musa alone narrated it."
"1090","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalaf narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: No garment was dearer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than the shirt. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Abd al-Mumin alone narrated it."
"1091","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Unays narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever frightens this clan of the Ansar has frightened what is between these two — and he placed his palms on his sides."
"1092","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ashari, from his father, that two men disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he said to the claimant: Bring your proof. He had no proof. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the oath is upon him. The man cried out at that, saying: My right will go by his oath. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath intending thereby to wrongfully take the right of his brother, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify him, and for him is a painful punishment. When the man heard it, he refrained from the oath and acknowledged the right of the man. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah except Thabit; Jafar alone narrated it."
"1093","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Khattab ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari, from Maymun ibn Mihran, he said: I came to Safiyyah bint Shaybah and asked her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marry Maymunah while in ihram? She said: No; he married her while both were not in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Khattab."
"1094","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Dahma al-Basri, a truthful shaykh, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The swiftest obedience in reward is maintaining kinship ties; and the people of a house may be wicked, yet their wealth grows and their number increases, when they maintain their kinship ties; and the swiftest disobedience in punishment is transgression and treachery; and the immersing oath consumes wealth, diminishes kinship, and leaves homes desolate. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abu al-Dahma; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1095","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Dahma narrated to us, from Abu Zilal al-QasmalI, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has a tablet of green chrysolite, which He placed beneath the Throne; He wrote therein: I am Allah, there is no god but I, the Most Merciful of the merciful; I created some three hundred and ten-odd characteristics; whoever comes with one of them along with the testimony that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Zilal except Abu al-Dahma; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1096","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray witr upon his camel, and he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Zuhayr."
"1097","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Khattab ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his wives to perform tamattu, and ordered cows for them. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Khattab."
"1098","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the chest of Umar with his hand when he embraced Islam three times, saying: O Allah, remove what is in his chest of rancor, and replace it with faith — saying that three times. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Khalid ibn Abi Bakr."
"1099","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you dress, and when you perform ablution, begin with your right sides. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Zuhayr."
"1100","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Abu Shuayb had a butcher boy; when he saw the hardship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions, he commanded his boy to bring them meat sufficient for five, and sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Come to us as the fifth of five. So he came, and with them was a sixth. When they reached the door of Abu Shuayb, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You sent to me and to five, and this one followed us; if you permit him he will enter, otherwise he will return. He said: I have permitted; let him enter, O Messenger of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, except Zuhayr."
"1101","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ufayr ibn Madan narrated to us, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the khuffs and the turban in the campaign of Tabuk. No one narrated this hadith from Sulaym except Ufayr; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1102","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ayyub al-Mawsili narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifah, from Abdullah ibn Dhakwan, from Ibn Umar, he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the sacrificial animals among us were camels and cows. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Umar."
"1103","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray in the Kabah, but when he entered he fell prostrate, then raised his head, then supplicated. Al-Fadl ibn Abbas narrated that to me, and he was with him when he entered. He said: And Ibn Abbas used to say: I do not like to pray in it; had I done so, I would have left part of the qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ishaq except Muhammad ibn Salamah."
"1104","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning this verse: But if they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them; and if you judge, judge between them with justice; indeed Allah loves the just — he said: They were of Banu al-Nadir; when they killed one slain from Banu Qurayzah they paid them half the blood-money, while Banu Qurayzah, when they killed one slain from Banu al-Nadir, paid them the full blood-money. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) equalized the full blood-money between them."
"1105","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Sayyid ibn Isa al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: From raisins, dates, wheat, and barley comes wine. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except al-Sayyid."
"1106","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: The first to recognize the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the defeat, when people said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been killed — as al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik, he said: Kab said: I recognized his eyes shining from beneath the helmet, so I called out at the top of my voice: O company of Muslims, this is the Messenger of Allah. So he gestured to me to be silent. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad."
"1107","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Shubah, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives with a single washing. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Miskin."
"1108","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah narrated to us, he said: I heard my grandfather Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, that he heard Abu Mahdhurah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast the adhan upon me letter by letter: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"1109","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mistresses of the women of Paradise — after Maryam daughter of Imran — are Fatimah and Khadijah, then Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except al-Darawardi, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"1110","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Isa ibn Sinan, from al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Arzab al-Ashari, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: I brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) water for ablution, and he wiped over the socks, the sandals, and the turban. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Isa alone narrated it."
"1111","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir al-Ramli narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting, he would break fast with milk; and I brought him a cup of milk, and placed it beside him, and he covered it while he was praying. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1112","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir al-Ramli narrated to us, from Asim ibn Talhah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make tharid, even with water. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Abbad alone narrated it."
"1113","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Of whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him. No one narrated this hadith from Idris except Ikrimah; al-Nufayli alone narrated it."
"1114","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Hud ibn Ata, he said: I heard Shaddad Abu Ammar say: I heard Abu Umamah say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say of a man who seeks good and repute — what does he get? He said: Nothing for him — saying that three times. Allah Blessed and Exalted does not accept of deeds except what is sincere for Him and sought for His sake. No one narrated this hadith from Hud except Muawiyah; Uthman alone narrated it."
"1115","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, that Aishah narrated to him, she said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a black khamisah; when his pain intensified, he would place it once upon his face, and once uncover it, saying: May Allah fight the people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques — warning his ummah of that."
"1116","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir al-Ramli narrated to us, from Shumaysah bint Nabhan, from her freedman Muslim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledging allegiance to women in the year of the Conquest upon al-Safa; and a woman came whose hand was like the hand of a man, and he refused to pledge her until she went and changed her hand with yellow dye; and a man came to him with an iron ring on his hand, and he said: Allah has not purified a hand in which there is an iron ring."
"1117","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Unays narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Sabrah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit one day, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then said: O people, there is no prayer without ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it; and he has not believed in Allah who has not believed in me; and he has not believed in me who has not recognized the right of the Ansar. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Sabrah except with this chain."
"1118","Ahmad narrated: ....."
"1119","... one of them erases a sin, and the other raises a degree. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I intended to command the prayer to be established. And he mentioned the hadith. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to outbid his brother, and forbade najsh (false bidding), and forbade a woman to ask for the divorce of her sister, and forbade withholding water for fear of pasture, and forbade a townsman to sell for a Bedouin. And he said: Whoever grants a milch animal, its morning milk and evening milk come as charity."
"1120","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of the Trench: They distracted us from the Asr prayer — and he did not pray it that day until the sun had set — may Allah fill their graves with fire, and their hearts with fire, and their houses with fire."
"1121","And from Zayd, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara, from his father, he said: I met my uncle — and with him was a banner — and I said: Where are you going? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married the wife of his father, and commanded me to strike his neck and take his wealth."
"1122","And from Zayd, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the refuse heap of a people and urinated; so I brought him water, and poured it over him; so he performed ablution and wiped his head, and wiped over his khuffs; then he stood and prayed."
"1123","And from Zayd, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: I asked Ubayy ibn Kab about the two Muawwidhatayn, and he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them, and he said: It was said to me, so I said. Ubayy said: Then he said to us, so we said."
"1124","And from Zayd, from Asim, from Khaythamah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then there will come a people whose oaths precede their testimony, and their testimony their oaths."
"1125","And from Zayd, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: I asked Ubayy ibn Kab about the Night of Decree, and he said: It is the night of the twenty-seventh, by the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us of: that the sun rises that morning without rays."
"1126","And from Asim, from Zirr, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi and asked him about wiping over the khuffs; so he said: When we traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he commanded us not to remove our khuffs for three nights and their days, except from janabah; but from stool and urine, no. And he mentioned the hadith."
"1127","And from Zayd, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever eats with a people, let him not join dates together; and if he wishes to do so, let him seek permission; and if they permit him, let him do so."
"1128","And from Zayd, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Abdi, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah al-Sadusi, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, and he stipulated upon me: that you bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; and you pray the five, and fast Ramadan, and pay zakah, and perform Hajj to the House, and strive in the path of Allah. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, as for two of them I cannot bear them: for by Allah, I have nothing but ten milch camels, the providers and mounts of my family; and as for jihad, they claim that whoever turns back incurs the anger of Allah, and I fear that when fighting comes my soul will be greedy and hate death. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grasped his hand, then moved it, then said: No charity and no jihad — then with what will you enter Paradise? So I pledged allegiance to him upon all of them."
"1129","And from Zayd, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing unripe dates and ripe dates."
"1130","And from Ibn Umar, he said: The companions of your Prophet used to dislike wearing silk and bringing it into their houses."
"1131","And from Zayd, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Nasr — Abu al-Qasim said: He is Humayd ibn Hilal — from Abu Barzah, he said: Abu Bakr became angry at a man with severe anger, until his color changed; and Abu Bakr was a man in whom there was sharpness. Abu Barzah said: When I saw that from him, I said: O caliph of the Messenger of Allah, if you command me, I shall strike his neck. So it was as if cold water had been poured upon him; his anger toward the man went away, and he said: May your mother bereave you, O Abu Barzah; it was not for anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1132","And with it: from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: The prophets were shown to me; and a prophet would come with none but one man with him, and another would come with none but two men with him, and a prophet would come with none but a small group likewise; and my ummah was shown to me, so I raised my head, and behold, the hillocks had filled between me and the horizon."
"1133","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Muwarriq al-Ijli, from Ibn Umar, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he asked for drink; so a cup containing nabidh was brought; and when he brought it close to his mouth he saw severity in it, so he returned it. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail, from Muwarriq, except Ubaydullah."
"1134","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, there will be tribulation, and your people will dispute with you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me? He said: Judge by the Book — or he said: Follow the Book. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ata; Ubayd alone narrated it."
"1135","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Rawh ibn Zinba, he said: I entered upon Tamim al-Dari while he was governor over Bayt al-Maqdis, and he was cleaning barley for his horse. So I said: O amir, did you have no one to suffice you this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever cleans barley for his horse in the path of Allah, then stands with it until he feeds it to him, Allah Almighty writes for him a good deed for every grain of barley. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Ibn Shawdhab, nor from Ibn Shawdhab except Ata; Ubayd alone narrated it."
"1136","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ata narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Abu Salih, he said: Umar arrived at al-Jabiyah, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Preserve my regard with respect to my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad except Ata; Ubayd alone narrated it."
"1137","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Yazid al-Kindi, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man performing ablution, washing his khuffs; so he nudged him with his foot and said: This is not the sunnah; we were commanded to wipe over the khuffs, like this — and he passed his hands over his khuffs. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Baqiyyah alone narrated it."
"1138","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he prayed over a dead person, he said: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, and our males and our females, and our young and our old; whomsoever You keep alive among us, keep him alive upon Islam; and whomsoever You cause to die among us, cause him to die upon faith; O Allah, Your pardon, Your pardon. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except al-Ala; Ata alone narrated it."
"1139","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a Muslim woman was taken by the enemy — and they had earlier taken a she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and she saw heedlessness from the people, so she mounted the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and vowed to slaughter the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah. He said: Evil is what you rewarded her with; there is no vow for the son of Adam concerning what he does not own, nor concerning disobedience to Allah."
"1140","And from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you swear an oath, then see better than it, do what is better, and expiate your oath; and do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it upon asking, you will be entrusted to it; and if you are given it without asking, you will be aided in it."
"1141","And from Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with perfume containing musk at his ihram before he entered ihram, and on the day of sacrifice before he circumambulated the House."
"1142","And from Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from me; Allah has made a way for them: the previously married with the previously married — one hundred lashes and stoning; and the virgin with the virgin — one hundred lashes and exile for a year."
"1143","And from Mansur, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Yazid ibn Sharik, from Abu Dharr, concerning His saying: And he certainly saw him on the clear horizon — he said: He saw him with his heart, and did not see him with his sight. No one narrated these hadiths from Mansur except Hushaym."
"1144","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar, Mughirah, Husayn, Mujalid, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, Ashath, and Dawud ibn Abi Hind all informed me, all from al-Shabi, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O daughter of Qays, lodging and maintenance are only for one whose return (of divorce) is possible."
"1145","And with it: Sayyar informed me, from al-Shabi, from Jarir, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Upon what do you pledge allegiance to me? I said: Upon hearing and obeying. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dictated to me: As much as you are able, and sincere advice to every Muslim."
"1146","And with it: Sayyar informed us, from Ibn Hubayrah, from Jabir, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he bought a camel from me; so I sold it to him on condition that its back remain mine until arrival. When we arrived, I brought him the camel, and he ordered its price for me; then he said: It is yours. So I went off with it, and a Jewish man met me, and I informed him; and he kept marveling, saying: He gave you the price and gifted you the camel? I said: Yes. No one narrated these hadiths from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam except Hushaym."
"1147","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Amr, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Awf ibn Malik al-Ashjai, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded wiping over the khuffs, in the campaign of Tabuk, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night. This hadith is not narrated from Awf except with this chain; Hushaym alone narrated it."
"1148","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qust narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"1149","And from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me in an illness I suffered; so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have none but a daughter of mine; shall I bequeath all my wealth in the path of Allah? He said: A third, and a third is much; that you leave your heirs rich is better than leaving them dependent, begging people with their hands; and you will not spend any expenditure seeking thereby the face of Allah but you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to the mouth of your wife; and perhaps Allah will raise you, so that some people will benefit through you and others will be harmed through you. Then he said: O Allah, complete for my Companions their emigration. But the wretched Sad ibn Khawlah — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pitied him for dying in Makkah."
"1150","And from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his companions the fear prayer. And he mentioned the hadith."
"1151","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qust narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be dearer to him than all else; and that he hate to return to disbelief as he hates to be cast into the Fire; and that he love a man loving him only for Allah Almighty. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Ubaydullah."
"1152","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to enter ihram, he would wash his head with khatmi, then oil it with some oil, not much."
"1153","And with it: she said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Pilgrimage; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah for his wives and left me; so I felt distressed, and said: O Messenger of Allah, you performed Umrah for your wives and left me. He said: O Abd al-Rahman, go out with your sister to al-Tanim, then let her circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, then let her shorten, then come to me before I depart — and that was on the night of al-Hasbah. Aishah said: He stayed the night of al-Hasbah only for my sake."
"1154","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Nawfal, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar — may Allah forgive her; and Aslam — may Allah grant her peace. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Ubaydullah."
"1155","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Mujahid, from Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be disagreement at the death of a caliph; so a man from Banu Hashim will go out and come to Makkah; and the people will bring him out of his house while he is unwilling, and pledge allegiance to him between the Corner and the Station; and an army from Syria will be dispatched toward him, until when they are at al-Bayda they will be swallowed; then the bands of Iraq and the substitutes of Syria will come to him; and a man will arise in Syria whose maternal uncles are Kalb, and an army will be dispatched toward him, and Allah will defeat them; so the rout will be upon them; and that is the day of Kalb; the loser is he who loses the spoils of Kalb; so he will conquer the treasures, and distribute wealth, and Islam will settle with its chest upon the earth; and he will live thereby seven years — or he said: nine years. Ubaydullah ibn Amr said: So I narrated it to Layth, and he said: Mujahid narrated it to me. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar except Ubaydullah."
"1156","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Fulfulah al-Jufi, he said: We were with Hudhayfah, and one of us said to him: Narrate to us, O Abu Abdullah, what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Had I done so, you would stone me. We said: Glory be to Allah, would we do that to you? He said: What would you say had I narrated to you that one of your mothers comes to you in a numerous battalion, severe in might, fighting you — would you believe me? They said: Glory be to Allah, who would believe that? So Hudhayfah said: The reddish one will come to you in a battalion driven by its non-Arabs from whence they drive their faces. Then he stood and entered a chamber of his."
"1157","And from Zayd, from Abu Amr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A people will enter Hell, then come out, and enter Paradise; they will be known therein by their names; they will be called: the Hell-dwellers."
"1158","And from Zayd, from Zayd ibn Rufay, from Hizam ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded women to give charity and urged them to it, saying: Give charity, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire. A woman among them said: Why is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because you curse much, and delay good, and are ungrateful to the husband."
"1159","And from Zayd, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five rakahs for Zuhr or Asr. So it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been increased? He said: No. They said: You prayed five with us. So he faced the qiblah and prostrated two prostrations while sitting, then saluted; then he said: These two prostrations are for one who thinks he added or omitted in his prayer."
"1160","And from Zayd, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara, he said: My uncle Hani ibn Niyar slaughtered his sacrifice before going out to prayer; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to repeat another sacrifice in its place. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a young goat better than an old one. He said: Sacrifice it, but it will not suffice for anyone after you."
"1161","With the same chain: from Jabir, from Nafi who said: We came to Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd and she narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I used to think that if anyone were to be exempted from the squeezing of the grave, Sad ibn Muadh would have been exempted; he was indeed squeezed once."
"1162","With the same chain: from Jabir, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah led us in prayer and stood up in the first two rakahs, so we glorified Allah to alert him, and he gestured with his hand meaning stand, so we stood; when he finished his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting after having given salam, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did likewise and said: If one remembers before standing fully upright, let him sit back, and if he does not remember until he is fully upright, let him continue his prayer, then prostrate two prostrations after the taslim."
"1163","And from Zayd, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: While we were walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he passed by boys playing, among them a boy, and it was as if that angered the Messenger of Allah, so he said to him: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? He replied: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? So he said: Be despised, for you will never exceed your measure. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike his neck. He said: O Umar, if he is the one you fear, you will never be able to kill him."
"1164","With the same chain: from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah who said: We were walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a snake appeared; we rushed toward it, and it entered a hole, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were protected from its evil, and it was protected from your evil."
"1165","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: We were young men with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to us: Whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity, and whoever cannot afford it, upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him."
"1166","And from Zayd, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Waddak Jabr ibn Nawf who said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the conquest of Hunayn, and we captured slave women, and we would practice withdrawal from them, so some of us said to others: You do this while the Messenger of Allah is among you? If only you asked him. So we asked him, and he said: Not from all fluid is the child; it is only something that when Allah wills it to be, it is, and no one can turn it back."
"1167","And from Zayd, from Yahya ibn al-Husayn, from his grandmother Umm al-Husayn who said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Hajj, and I saw Bilal and Usamah, Bilal holding the halter of his mount, and the other lifting his garment to shade him from the heat, until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah; then he turned and had placed his garment under his right armpit over his left shoulder, and I saw the edge of his right shoulder like a gathered mass; he stood before the people and said many words, among what he said was: If a black slave with amputated limbs is placed in authority over you and leads you by the Book of Allah, listen to him and obey."
"1168","And from Zayd, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ala ibn Arar who said: Ibn Umar was asked about Ali and Uthman, and he said: As for Ali, do not ask about him; look at his position with the Messenger of Allah, for he closed our doors to the mosque and left his door open; and as for Uthman, he committed a great sin on the day the two armies met, but Allah pardoned him, and he committed a lesser sin against you, yet you killed him."
"1169","And from Zayd, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad who said: Two angels came to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them said: Recite the Quran upon one letter. The other said: Add more for him. He kept asking for more until he said: Recite the Quran upon seven letters."
"1170","And from Zayd, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his brother Abdullah ibn Kab, from Abu Umamah al-Harithi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man without right, Allah the Mighty and Majestic forbids Paradise to him and makes the Fire obligatory for him. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something small? He said: Even if it is a siwak stick of arak wood."
"1171","With the same chain: from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the believer is to the middle of his shins, and there is no sin upon him in what is between that and the ankles, and whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him."
"1172","And from Zayd, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami who said: When Uthman was besieged, he looked down upon them from above his house and said: I remind you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the army of hardship: Whoever spends an accepted expenditure - while the people that day were strained and in hardship - so I equipped a third of that army from my wealth? They said: Yes. He said: I remind you by Allah, do you know Rumah, from which no one would drink except for a price, so I bought it with my wealth and made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer? They said: Yes, among other things he listed."
"1173","With the same chain: from Abu Ishaq, from Zaidah ibn Umayr who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about withdrawal, and he said: You have talked much about it. If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything about it, it is as he said, and if he did not say anything about it, then I say about it: Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish; if you wish then practice withdrawal, and if you wish then do not practice withdrawal."
"1174","With the same chain: from Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever keeps a horse tied in the path of Allah, its fodder and its traces are in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."
"1175","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Nafi who said: Ibn Umar was on a journey and heard the sound of a flute, so he placed his two fingers in his ears and turned away from the road, then said: O Nafi, do you hear? I said: No, so he returned to the road, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"1176","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Thabit, a companion of al-Hasan, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who serves drink to the people is the last of them to drink."
"1177","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qust narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took meat from a shoulder and ate, then prayed without performing ablution. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ishaq ibn Rashid."
"1178","With the same chain: from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting At-Tur in Maghrib."
"1179","And from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding nabidh of gourds and varnished vessels."
"1180","With the same chain: from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, both of us in a state of janabah."
"1181","And from al-Zuhri, from Salim and Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you are told that the plague has struck a land, do not come to it, and if it strikes a land while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it."
"1182","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal and Mughirah, both from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Zamzam and drank while standing. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Hushaym."
"1183","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi who said: Ibn Umar was asked about walls containing filth, human urine, and animal dung. He said: When rains flow over them and winds dry them, there is no harm in praying there, mentioning that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Musa; Amr alone narrated it from him."
"1184","Ahmad ibn Mutayr al-Ramli the judge narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Mashar, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The supplication of the oppressed is not rejected even if he is wicked; his wickedness is upon himself. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abd al-Razzaq; Ibn Abi al-Sari alone narrated it from him."
"1185","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Mamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dawud (peace be upon him) would eat only from the earnings of his hand. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except al-Walid; Muhammad alone narrated it from him."
"1186","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Umayyah ibn Zayd, from Abu Musabbih al-Maqrai, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The head of the religion is sincere advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah the Mighty and Majestic, to His religion, to His Book, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to the Muslims in general. This hadith is not narrated from Thawban except with this chain; Ayyub alone narrated it."
"1187","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn ibn Sad narrated to us, from Sharahil ibn Yazid al-Maafiri, from Ubayd ibn Amr al-Asbahi, from Abu Hurayrah that Anas ibn Malik informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would gesture in prayer. We do not know that Abu Hurayrah narrated from Anas any hadith other than this one, and this has been narrated from Anas through other chains."
"1188","Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Jarir ibn Jabalah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi, from Amir al-Shabi, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: Whoever is pleased to read the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him read these verses: Say, come, I will recite what your Lord has forbidden you, up to His saying: This He has enjoined upon you that you may become righteous. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except Dawud; Muhammad ibn Fudayl alone narrated it from him."
"1189","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Salim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked her: Who is proposing to Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah? She said: So-and-so and so-and-so, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. He said: Marry her to Abd al-Rahman, for he is among the best of the Muslims, and among the best of them is whoever is like him. This hadith is not narrated from Busrah except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"1190","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The prayer would be established, then a man would intercept the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and speak to him about a need, detaining him until some of the people dozed."
"1191","With the same chain: from Anas that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold."
"1192","With the same chain: from Anas who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan, and he fasted and his Companions fasted with him; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast, and some of his Companions broke fast with him, while some of them fasted, and the fasting one was better than the breaking one."
"1193","With the same chain: from Anas that he was asked about old women, did they attend prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, and young women; they would pray behind our shoulders with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Aishah said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had seen what women are upon today, he would not have left them. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Amash except Khalid."
"1194","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Bayan al-Shulathai narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Mansur and al-Amash and Ubaydah ibn Mutib and Habib ibn Hassan, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch some of his wives while he was fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Sayf."
"1195","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mutarrif al-Mughirah ibn Mutarrif al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from Muawiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of Ashura and said: This is a day whose fasting has not been written upon you, so whoever wishes may fast. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abu al-Mutarrif; Bishr alone narrated it from him."
"1196","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah Muhammad ibn Firas al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad that Abu Usayd, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), married a woman and invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his wedding; his wife, though the bride, would stand over us and give us date-nabidh to drink, which she had soaked in the night and strained. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman except Abu Qutaybah."
"1197","Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Firdawsi narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man whose cousin comes to him asking from his surplus and he withholds it from him, Allah will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever withholds water to thereby withhold the surplus of pasture, Allah will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Jarir; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan alone narrated it from him."
"1198","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sad narrated to me that he heard Ibn Tawus saying: I heard Tawus saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Attach wealth to the prescribed shares, and what remains is for the closest male. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Yusuf."
"1199","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ziyad narrated to me, from Utbah al-Kufi, from Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finds a louse in the mosque, let him bury it or remove it from himself. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ziyad except Yusuf; his son alone narrated them from him."
"1200","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that he passed by people who had set up a chicken shooting at it, so he took it away and said: Whoever takes anything possessing a soul as a target will not die from this world until a calamity strikes him. Simak narrated nothing from Nafi other than this."
